/* interpretations.js — classic script; assigns to window.TD. No ES modules, so file:// works.
   Sample interpretations for every card, written for this demo in plain modern English:
   up / rev (the general reading), loveUp / loveRev, workUp / workRev (work and money), and picture
   (what is on the 1909 Pamela Colman Smith card and what it suggests).
   Written fresh for this demo against the traditional Rider-Waite-Smith meanings, with A.E. Waite's
   1911 text (js/data/meanings.js) as the reference. Not copied from any site or book.
   On a live site the reader edits these or replaces them with their own words, card by card. */
window.TD = window.TD || {};
window.TD.READINGS = {"major-00":{"up":"You are standing at the start of something, and you do not have the full map yet. That is the point. A new job, a move, a first date, a project you keep sketching in the margins: the moment asks you to step forward with curiosity instead of waiting for every answer. There is a wild, slightly reckless streak here too, the part of you that would rather try and stumble than play it safe forever. Let that energy carry you, but keep one eye open. Enthusiasm is a gift when it moves you, and a problem only when it replaces paying attention. Pack light, trust your feet, and let yourself be a beginner again.","rev":"Something new is calling, and either you keep hovering at the edge or you have already jumped without looking. Both come from the same place: not quite being present with the choice. Maybe fear of looking foolish has you frozen, rehearsing the first step until the chance goes stale. Or maybe carelessness has crept in, and you are rushing past details that matter because thinking about them feels boring. Notice which one sounds like you right now. The fix is not to give up on the adventure. It is to slow down long enough to actually choose it, check the ground, and then move with your eyes open rather than shut.","loveUp":"Fresh energy is moving through your love life. If you are single, say yes to the unexpected invitation or the person who is not your usual type, and let it be light for a while. If you are partnered, bring some play back in: a spontaneous day out, a new thing you try together. Nobody needs a five-year plan tonight.","loveRev":"Watch for two opposite habits. One is holding back so long that a promising connection never gets a real chance. The other is diving into something intense before you know whether the other person is on the same page. Whether you are dating or in a relationship, slow down, ask what you actually want, and let the other person answer for themselves.","workUp":"A new direction at work is opening, maybe a role you feel underqualified for or an idea nobody has tried yet. You do not need to be an expert to begin. Bring your curiosity, ask the naive questions, and be willing to learn in public. Just decide how much time and energy you will give it before the excitement decides for you.","workRev":"Either you are stalling on a fresh start at work or charging ahead without the groundwork. A plan that lives only in your head is not quite a plan yet, and a leap with no research behind it can cost more than it should. Take one practical step today: a conversation, a draft, a checklist. Momentum and care can go together.","picture":"A young traveler strides toward the edge of a rocky cliff, his face lifted to a bright yellow sky and a white sun. A black staff rests on his shoulder with a small red bag tied to its end, and his other hand holds a white rose. His dark green tunic is patterned with red roundels, and a red feather sits in his cap. A white dog leaps at his heels, and snowy peaks rise behind him. He is looking up, not down. The light pack and the rose suggest innocence and trust, while the dog seems to be either cheering him on or warning him about the drop."},
"major-01":{"up":"Everything you need to get this started is already within reach. The skills, the contacts, the tools, the idea: they are on the table in front of you, and the moment asks you to pick them up and use them with intent. You have a gift right now for turning a thought into something real, and for saying the right thing to the right person at the right time. Confidence comes from doing, so start. Pick one clear aim and point all your attention at it. Attention is your sharpest tool. Be honest with yourself about your motives, too, because skill used cleverly and skill used well are not always the same.","rev":"The talent is there, but it is not landing. Maybe you have several projects half begun and none finished, or you keep talking about the plan while the actual work waits. Energy scattered across ten directions ends up moving nothing very far. There can also be a restless, uneasy feeling underneath, a sense that you are performing competence rather than feeling it. Watch, too, for cleverness that slides into spin, whether it is yours or someone else's. Bring it back to one task, one honest intention and one next action. When your words and your hands start doing the same thing again, the power returns.","loveUp":"You have more say in your love life than you might think. If you are single, show up as yourself, start the conversation, make the plan. If you are with someone, say clearly what you want and put effort behind it. Attraction grows when words and actions match, and right now you have a knack for making both count.","loveRev":"Be wary of charm that has no follow-through, including your own. Someone may be saying all the right things while showing very little, or you may be playing a role to be liked. Whether you are dating or settled, look at actions over promises, and ask yourself what you would say if you were not trying to impress.","workUp":"Now is a strong moment to make something happen at work. Pitch the idea, build the prototype, lead the meeting. You have the skills and the resources, and people are likely to respond to clear, confident communication. Choose a single goal and put your full attention on it rather than spreading yourself across everything at once.","workRev":"Busy is not the same as productive. If your to-do list is long and your results are thin, look for where effort is leaking: too many projects, too much talk, not enough finishing. Be careful, too, with anyone whose pitch sounds polished but vague. Narrow down, deliver one solid piece of work, and let that speak.","picture":"A young man in a white tunic and a flowing red robe stands behind a wooden table, one arm raised to hold a white wand toward the sky while his other hand points down at the earth. A sideways figure eight floats above his dark hair. On the table lie a golden cup, a disc marked with a star and a sword. Red roses hang from vines overhead, and more roses and white lilies grow at his feet against a yellow background. The pose links above and below, as if he is a channel between an idea and its making."},
"major-02":{"up":"Some answers do not arrive by thinking harder. They surface when you get quiet enough to hear them. You may already sense the truth of a situation even if you cannot yet explain it, and the moment asks you to trust that knowing rather than argue it away. Not everything is ready to be revealed. There may be facts still hidden, or a future still taking shape, and forcing a conclusion now would only get in the way. Keep your own counsel for a while. Notice dreams, hunches and the small detail that keeps nagging at you. Silence can be a strength, and patience here is its own kind of wisdom.","rev":"You probably know more than you are letting yourself admit. It is easy to drown out a quiet instinct with busyness, other people's opinions, or a strong feeling that looks like certainty but is really just heat. Watch for the urge to act on surface information, or to believe you have figured someone out after one conversation. Secrets can play a part as well. If you have been holding something in for too long, it may be weighing on you more than sharing it would. Make some time alone, without your phone, and ask yourself a direct question. Then take the answer seriously.","loveUp":"Pay attention to what your intuition is telling you about a person, even if nothing has been said out loud. If you are single, there may be quiet interest around you that you have not noticed yet. If you are partnered, some understanding runs deeper than words. Let things unfold at their own pace rather than pushing for a label.","loveRev":"Something unspoken is shaping your love life. Maybe you are ignoring a gut feeling about how someone treats you, or keeping a feeling hidden so long that it has become a wall. Whether you are single or partnered, honesty with yourself comes first. Then decide, with care, what needs to be said aloud.","workUp":"Hold your cards close for now. Not every plan needs to be announced, and there may be information at work you do not yet have. Listen more than you speak in meetings, read between the lines, and trust your sense of who and what is reliable. Quiet preparation will serve you better than a big reveal.","workRev":"Your instincts about a work situation deserve a hearing. If a new arrangement or project feels off, do not wave that away just because it looks good on paper. On the other hand, be careful with office secrets and gossip, which tend to create confusion. Get the facts, check your sources, and trust the thoughtful part of you.","picture":"A woman sits calmly between two pillars, a black one marked B and a white one marked J. She wears flowing pale blue robes with a white cross on her chest and a crown shaped like horns cradling a round disc. A scroll rests half hidden in her lap under the fold of her cloak. Behind her hangs a veil patterned with palm leaves and pomegranates, and a golden crescent moon lies at her feet. Her face is still and unreadable. She guards a threshold, holding what is known on one side and what is hidden on the other."},
"major-03":{"up":"Life wants to grow around you right now, and you are invited to tend it. Ideas, friendships, a garden, a creative project, your own well-being: whatever you pour care into is likely to flourish. Pay attention to your body and your senses too. Good food, rest, time outside and small comforts are not indulgences at the moment, they are fuel. There is also a practical side here. Growth still takes initiative, so take the first step on the thing you want to nurture instead of waiting for perfect conditions. A little doubt may come along for the ride. Keep watering anyway, and trust that steady care brings real results.","rev":"Care has gone lopsided. Perhaps you are giving so much to other people or projects that your own tank is empty, or perhaps your support has turned into hovering, and the person or plan you love needs more room to breathe. Either way, something is out of balance. Notice where you have stopped eating well, resting, or making things for the joy of it. You may also be wavering, unable to commit to what you want to grow. The good news is that tangled situations often loosen once you tend to yourself again. Put your own needs back on the list, then see what looks clearer.","loveUp":"Warmth and affection come easily now. If you are in a relationship, small acts of care, a cooked meal or an unhurried evening, will deepen your bond. If you are single, focus on feeling good in your own skin, and let your openness draw people who appreciate it. Love grows best when you are nourished too.","loveRev":"Watch for giving until you have nothing left, or for care that crosses into control. A partner or a date is not a project to manage. If you are single, you may have been neglecting yourself while waiting to be chosen. Turn some of that tenderness inward, and let relationships breathe rather than holding them too tightly.","workUp":"Projects you have nurtured are ready to show real growth. It is a good time for creative work, mentoring, and anything that benefits from a patient, generous approach. Make your workspace comfortable and pleasant, and take the initiative on ideas that feel alive. Results come from steady tending more than from pressure.","workRev":"You may be carrying everyone else's workload or micromanaging something that needs space to develop. Creativity dries up when you are running on empty. Step back, delegate where you can, and restore your energy. Indecision could be holding a project in limbo, so choose what deserves your care and let the rest wait.","picture":"A fair-haired woman sits at ease on soft red and orange cushions, wearing a crown of stars over a green wreath and a loose white gown scattered with red fruit. She holds a golden scepter in one hand. Beside her rests a heart-shaped shield bearing the symbol of Venus. Tall ripe wheat fills the foreground, dark evergreens rise behind her, and a stream spills down on the right under a golden sky. Everything around her is growing, ripening or flowing, and she seems perfectly comfortable in the middle of it."},
"major-04":{"up":"Order is your friend right now. Things work better when there is a clear structure: a schedule, a set of agreements, a boundary you actually keep. You may be stepping into authority yourself, taking charge of a situation that needs a steady hand, or you may be dealing with someone who holds that role for you. Either way, clear thinking and firm conviction are more useful than feelings alone. Build the frame first, and the rest has somewhere to live. Protection belongs here too. Good leadership keeps people safe and plans ahead. Decide what matters, set your terms, and follow through with the kind of consistency that earns trust.","rev":"Structure has turned into a cage. Maybe rules that once kept things steady now just keep them stuck, or someone, possibly you, is holding on to control long after it stopped helping. Stubbornness can look like strength from the inside. There may also be the opposite problem: a lack of discipline, or authority exercised in a way that feels immature and reactive. Ask where you are gripping too hard and where you have let things drift. The way forward often involves more compassion than you expect. Loosen your hold a little, listen to the people affected, and rebuild a structure that serves everyone, including you.","loveUp":"Stability and commitment are highlighted. In a relationship, now is a time for clear agreements and showing up reliably. If you are single, know your standards and hold to them. Someone steady and dependable may appeal to you more than a thrill. Security can be romantic when two people build it freely.","loveRev":"Look for where control is creeping into love. One partner may be making all the decisions, or rules are replacing warmth. If you are single, a rigid checklist could be screening out good people. Soften the edges. Protection and care matter, but so does room for each person to be themselves.","workUp":"Take the lead and put things in order. Create systems, set clear expectations, and make decisions based on reason rather than mood. You may be backed by a strong manager, or you may be the one others look to for direction. Solid planning now lays groundwork that lasts.","workRev":"Rigid rules, a controlling boss, or your own need to control everything may be slowing things down. Ask whether a process still serves its purpose or just protects someone's authority. Leadership also means listening. A little flexibility and kindness will get more done than doubling down on the chain of command.","picture":"An older king with a long white beard sits on a square stone throne carved with ram heads on its arms and upper corners. He wears a gold crown and a red robe over a suit of armor that shows at his legs. In one hand he holds an ankh-shaped scepter, in the other a golden orb. Behind him rise bare orange mountains under a red-orange sky. There is nothing soft here, only stone, metal and firm lines. The armor under the robe hints that his rule is backed by a readiness to defend what he has built."},
"major-05":{"up":"There is wisdom in the road that others have already walked. You may be drawn toward a tradition, a teacher, a community or an established way of doing things, and it can offer real guidance right now. Learning the rules before bending them is not weakness. It is how skill is built. Look for a mentor or trusted adviser you can turn to, someone whose experience you respect. Commitments made in this spirit, like a partnership, a course of study or a formal agreement, tend to be solid. Just notice the line between support and captivity. Belonging should give you strength, not ask you to shrink.","rev":"The old rulebook may not fit anymore. You might feel restless inside a tradition, a family expectation, or an institution that once gave you a sense of place and now mostly gives you a list of shoulds. It is fine to question. Watch for the other side too: going along with the group to keep the peace, being so agreeable that your own voice disappears. Harmony is lovely, but not at the cost of honesty. Ask which beliefs you chose and which ones you simply inherited. You get to keep the parts that still feel true and gently set down the rest. Your path can be personal.","loveUp":"Commitment and shared values take center stage. In a relationship, now can be a time for deepening your bond or making a more formal promise. If you are single, connection may come through a community, a class or friends of friends. Steady, respectful pacing suits you right now.","loveRev":"Ask whether you are following your heart or a script. Family expectations, cultural rules or ideas about how love should look may be pressing on you. If you are single, you might be judging people by a checklist that is not really yours. In any relationship, find the arrangement that fits both of you.","workUp":"Established methods and good mentors are your best resources. It is a strong time for training, certification, joining a professional group or working within an organization's culture. Ask someone experienced, whose judgment you trust, for guidance. Following proven processes will help you build credibility before you innovate.","workRev":"Office bureaucracy or outdated procedures may be frustrating you. There is room to question how things have always been done, respectfully and with a better idea in hand. Be careful not to people-please at the expense of good judgment. Your fresh perspective has value even in a traditional setting.","picture":"A robed religious figure sits on a throne between two gray stone pillars. He wears a tall three-tiered gold crown and a red robe with a white stole marked with small crosses. His right hand is raised in blessing, and his left holds a golden staff topped with a triple cross. At his feet lie two crossed keys on a red checkered floor, and two kneeling figures with shaved crowns face him from below. The scene is formal and ordered, all about teaching that is passed down and received."},
"major-06":{"up":"A choice from the heart is in front of you, and it matters because it shows who you are. Love, attraction and beauty are all present, and they can point to a relationship that feels deeply right. Underneath the romance, though, sits a question about alignment: what do you truly value, and do your actions match it? Whether the decision concerns a person, a path or a promise, the right answer is the one you can stand behind fully. Harmony between two people, or between your head and your heart, grows from honesty. Any tests that come with it can be met and moved through. Choose with open eyes.","rev":"Something is out of step. Maybe your heart wants one thing and your choices keep pointing somewhere else, or you are putting off a decision in the hope it will make itself. It rarely does. Plans built on wishful thinking may stall, and frictions you have been smoothing over could come to the surface. None of this is final. It is information. Take an honest look at your values and ask where you have drifted from them. Sometimes the misalignment is inside a relationship, and sometimes it is between you and the life you are building. Making even a small, true choice starts bringing things back into line.","loveUp":"Connection runs deep right now. If you are in a relationship, you may feel a renewed sense of partnership and shared purpose. If you are single, you could feel a strong pull toward someone whose values match yours. Either way, love grows from honest choices made freely by both people.","loveRev":"A mismatch in values or timing may be causing tension. You might be avoiding a conversation about where things are going, or feeling torn between two paths. If you are single, check whether you are choosing people who truly fit you. Honesty, first with yourself, clears the way.","workUp":"A choice about your work path benefits from asking what you really value. A partnership or collaboration could be especially promising if you share the same goals. Make decisions from integrity rather than convenience, even when the easier option is tempting, and look for work that reflects who you are.","workRev":"Something at work does not sit right with your values, or a decision keeps getting pushed back. A partnership may be pulling in two directions. Rather than letting it drift, name the conflict clearly and weigh your options with care. Clarity will come from choosing, not waiting.","picture":"A large golden sun blazes at the top, and beneath it an angel with red wings and flame-like hair spreads both arms over the scene from a cloud. Below stand a man and a woman, both unclothed, on open ground. Behind the woman grows a tree heavy with red fruit, a serpent coiled around its trunk. Behind the man stands a tree whose leaves are small flames. Between them a tall pointed mountain rises under a pale green sky. The woman looks up toward the angel, the man looks at her, and the whole picture turns on trust, choice and being seen."},
"major-07":{"up":"You can get where you are going, as long as you keep both hands steady. Momentum is on your side, and a win is well within reach if you commit to a direction and stay with it. The challenge is that the forces pulling you are not all heading the same way. Doubts, competing priorities, other people's agendas: they need to be steered, not obeyed. Discipline and self-belief do most of the work here. There may be some struggle along the way, even a clash or two, but determination carries you through. Just keep an eye on overconfidence. Winning is sweeter when you have not run anyone over to get there.","rev":"Effort without direction is burning a lot of fuel. You may be pushing hard in several ways at once and getting nowhere, or trying to force a result that needs patience instead. Frustration can spill into arguments, and small disputes may be eating energy that should go into the actual goal. It can also feel like you have lost the reins altogether, with events steering you. Pause and ask where you are really trying to go. Which forces in your life are working against each other? Deal with that tension first. Once you have one direction and a calmer grip, progress comes back, often faster than you expect.","loveUp":"Take an active part in your love life. If you are single, go after the kind of connection you want by putting yourself out there with confidence. If you are partnered, work together toward a shared goal, like a move or a new routine. Steady commitment from both people moves a relationship forward.","loveRev":"Pushing too hard may be backfiring. Trying to control where a relationship goes, or clashing over who is in charge, can leave both people feeling stuck. If you are single, forcing chemistry rarely works. Ease off the pressure, talk about what each of you actually wants, and let the pace be mutual.","workUp":"Drive and focus can carry you to a real win at work. Set a clear goal, manage competing demands, and stay disciplined. Obstacles are likely, but you have the willpower to steer around them. Confidence and a steady hand will earn respect, especially under pressure.","workRev":"Busy but going in circles? Look for projects moving in opposite directions or conflicts with colleagues draining your drive. Forcing a deadline or a decision could create more friction. Step back, set priorities, and address disagreements directly and calmly. A clear course will get you further than raw effort.","picture":"A young man in armor stands in a stone chariot beneath a blue canopy scattered with stars. A star shines on his crown, crescent moons sit on his shoulders, and he holds a slim wand in one hand, with no reins in sight. In front of the chariot rest two sphinxes, one black and one white, both in striped headdresses. A winged disc decorates the front of the carriage. Behind him rise the walls and red roofs of a town under a yellow sky. He steers by will alone, keeping opposite forces moving as one."},
"major-08":{"up":"Being strong right now looks less like force and more like patience. It is the calm you keep while something wild settles down, whether that is a tense situation, another person's temper, or your own fear and frustration. You do not have to overpower it. Steady kindness and quiet courage will do more than pressure ever could. You have more inner resources than you might believe, and meeting a challenge with an open heart can turn it around. Energy and confidence are available to you, so use them with grace, and success tends to follow. Stay with it, even when progress feels slow. Soft power is still power.","rev":"Self-doubt may be louder than usual. You could be questioning whether you are capable of handling something, even though your track record says you are. Or the balance has tipped the other way, and you are trying to push through with force where patience would work better, snapping at people or muscling decisions. Both drain you. There might also be a power struggle nearby, someone throwing their weight around. Come back to your center. Breathe, rest, and remember that gentleness is not weakness. You do not have to prove anything by being hard. Rebuild your confidence slowly, and treat yourself with the same patience you would offer a friend.","loveUp":"Patience and compassion are your best tools in love now. If you are in a relationship, calm understanding can soothe a tense moment. If you are single, confidence that comes from self-acceptance is magnetic. Being gentle with your own heart helps you open it to someone else.","loveRev":"Insecurity or frustration may be spilling into your love life. Maybe you are doubting your worth, or someone is trying to dominate rather than share. Whether single or partnered, notice where force is replacing trust. Rebuild from self-respect, and do not accept being overpowered in any relationship.","workUp":"Quiet confidence will serve you better than aggression at work. Handle difficult colleagues or tough projects with patience and a steady temper. Your calm persistence will be noticed, and recognition can follow. Lead by example rather than by pressure, and trust that you are capable.","workRev":"Stress or self-doubt may be affecting your performance. Or you might be dealing with a heavy-handed boss, or trying to push projects through by sheer force. Neither works for long. Take a breath, reconnect with your skills, and choose patience over power plays. Small steady wins rebuild confidence.","picture":"A woman in a white gown bends over a red lion and gently holds its jaws with her hands. A figure-eight shape floats above her head, and she wears a wreath of flowers in her hair with a garland of roses around her waist, trailing toward the lion. The lion leans into her touch, its curly mane framing its face. Behind them are green trees, a distant blue mountain and a warm yellow sky. There is no struggle in her posture, only calm and trust, as if the taming happens through tenderness rather than strength of arm."},
"major-09":{"up":"Step back from the noise for a while. The answer you are looking for is more likely to come from reflection than from another round of advice or scrolling. Solitude now is not loneliness. It is a chance to hold one honest question up to the light and see what it shows you. Go slowly and carefully. Prudence serves you well here, especially before commitments or big decisions. Be discerning about what others present to you too, since not everything is as it appears, and a quiet eye catches what a busy one misses. Your inner guidance is steady, even if it only lights the next few steps.","rev":"Withdrawal has gone on a little too long. What started as healthy time alone may have become isolation, a way of keeping everyone at arm's length. You might be refusing help or advice because it feels safer to figure everything out by yourself. Caution is useful, but fear dressed as caution is something else. There may also be something you are hiding, from others or from yourself. Ask whether your distance is protecting you or just keeping you stuck. Reach out to one person you trust. Letting someone in, even a little, can bring back the light you have been missing.","loveUp":"Time alone may be exactly what your heart needs. If you are single, getting to know yourself deeply will clarify what you want in a partner. If you are in a relationship, space for personal reflection can strengthen the bond. Honest self-knowledge makes for honest love.","loveRev":"Pulling away from love out of fear may be keeping you lonely. If you are single, ask whether you are hiding from connection. If you are partnered, emotional distance could be growing. Share what you have been keeping inside, at a pace that feels safe, and let someone meet you there.","workUp":"Focused, independent work suits you now. Research, planning and deep thinking will pay off more than networking or quick moves. Consider seeking an experienced mentor, or becoming one for someone else. Take time to weigh decisions carefully, and look beyond surface appearances before trusting a new arrangement.","workRev":"Working in isolation may be limiting you. Refusing feedback or collaboration could slow your progress, and too much caution can mean missed chances. Share your ideas with a trusted colleague, ask for input, and step out of the background. Your insight is valuable when others can see it.","picture":"An old man in a long gray hooded cloak stands alone on a snowy peak. His head is bowed, his white beard just visible under the hood. In one raised hand he holds a lantern with a star-shaped light glowing inside, and in the other he grips a tall yellow staff. The background is a plain gray-green, empty of anything else. He is not looking far ahead, only at the ground in front of him. The lantern suggests guidance that shows the next step rather than the whole road."},
"major-10":{"up":"Things are moving, and not all of the movement is yours to control. A lucky break, a chance meeting, a door that opens just as you stopped pushing on it: life has a way of turning at its own speed, and right now the turn looks to be in your favor. Enjoy the lift. Say yes to the opportunity that arrives on its own schedule, and notice how timing seems to line up without much help from you. The deeper lesson is about holding things lightly. Good seasons pass and hard ones do too, so the wise move is to ride the rise with gratitude and use it well, without gripping it as if it has to last forever. Change is the one steady thing here.","rev":"The wheel has already moved, and part of you is still standing where it used to be. Maybe a situation changed and you keep acting as if it has not, or you are waiting for things to swing back to how they were. That waiting can keep you stuck. There may also be more going on than you can easily use: more options, more activity, more noise, and not all of it is worth chasing. Plenty is not the same as direction. Look at what has actually shifted and accept it as your new starting point. Then choose what to keep and what to let pass. Cycles keep turning, and you are better placed for the next one once you stop dragging your heels against this one.","loveUp":"Timing is working in your favor. If you are single, a meeting that seems like pure chance could turn out to matter, so keep saying yes to invitations. If you are in a relationship, you may be entering a new, lighter chapter together. Let the change happen rather than trying to schedule it, and enjoy the ease while it is here.","loveRev":"Love may be in a different season than you would like. Maybe a relationship has shifted and you are still hoping it will swing back, or you are dating out of habit rather than real interest. Respect where things actually stand, including other people's choices. If you are single, a quiet spell is not a verdict. Put your energy where you are welcome now.","workUp":"Doors at work may open with surprisingly little effort: a project lands on your desk, a contact remembers you, a change in the team moves you up. Be ready to step in when the chance comes. Treat good momentum as something to build on rather than something to count on, and keep your skills sharp for the next turn.","workRev":"A change at work has already happened, even if you are still treating it as temporary. A new manager, a shifted priority or a slower season calls for adapting rather than waiting. You may also have more on your plate than you can use well. Drop what no longer fits, and work with the conditions you actually have.","picture":"A large orange wheel fills the middle of the card against a blue-green sky. Its rim carries the letters T, A, R and O between Hebrew letters, and its spokes hold small symbols. A blue sphinx with a sword sits calmly on top. A yellow snake slides down the left side, while a red figure with a jackal's head rises on the right, carried upward by the turning. In the four corners, winged figures, an angel, an eagle, a bull and a lion, rest on clouds reading open books. Everything rises or falls with the wheel except the watchers, who stay steady and keep studying."},
"major-11":{"up":"Cause and effect are easy to see right now. Choices have consequences, and you are asked to look at yours, and at other people's, with clear and honest eyes. The balance tends to settle in favor of whoever has acted with integrity, so this is a good moment to tell the truth, keep your word and weigh a decision on its merits rather than on how you feel about the people involved. Fairness is not always comfortable. It may mean owning your part in something, or asking for what you are genuinely owed. Think it through, then act decisively. A clear, reasoned choice made now can set things straight in a way that holds up over time.","rev":"Something feels lopsided. Maybe you are being judged unfairly, or you are judging someone else, or yourself, far more harshly than the situation deserves. Bias can hide inside what feels like common sense, so check whether you have heard every side before you decide. Unfinished business, an unreturned favor or an unresolved argument, may still be sitting between people, and paperwork or official processes can feel tangled and slow. It is tempting to dodge responsibility or to make someone pay for more than their share. Neither brings peace. Look for where honesty has slipped, including in the story you tell yourself. Setting one small thing right, an apology or an overdue conversation, helps restore the balance.","loveUp":"Honesty and fairness hold love together now. If you are partnered, look at whether the give and take feels even, and talk about it plainly. If you are single, be truthful about what you want and what you offer. Clear choices, made with open eyes, lead to connections that feel balanced for both people.","loveRev":"An imbalance in love needs attention. One person may be giving more, or old resentments are being kept like a scorecard. If you are single, you might be judging new people by a past hurt. Whatever your situation, avoid blame for its own sake. Say what feels unfair, listen to the reply, and decide from there.","workUp":"Fair dealing tends to pay off at work right now. Keep careful records, honor your agreements and base decisions on facts. If you are negotiating or weighing an offer, look at it objectively. Colleagues notice integrity, and a reputation for being even-handed will serve you in whatever comes next.","workRev":"Something at work feels unfair: credit going to the wrong person, rules applied unevenly, or a process full of red tape. You may also be too hard on yourself or on a colleague. Stay factual, write down what matters, and raise concerns through fair channels. Getting even rarely helps, but getting clear usually does.","picture":"A crowned figure sits on a stone seat between two gray pillars, dressed in a deep red robe with a green cape fastened by a square clasp. The raised right hand holds an upright sword, its blade pointing straight up, and the left hand holds a set of golden scales low and steady. A red-purple curtain hangs behind the seat, with a band of yellow showing above it, and one white shoe peeks out beneath the hem. The figure looks straight out at you without expression. The sword suggests a clear decision, and the scales suggest it comes only after careful weighing."},
"major-12":{"up":"Progress may pause here, and that pause could be the most useful thing to happen to you in a while. When pushing gets you nowhere, stopping lets you notice what you missed. Try turning the problem upside down: what if the obstacle is the lesson, or the thing you are afraid to give up is the thing holding you back? Letting go of a small comfort or an old certainty can open a much bigger understanding. Your intuition is strong right now, so give it room. Waiting on purpose is different from being stuck. You are choosing to let things settle until you can see clearly, and that choice is a quiet form of wisdom.","rev":"The waiting has stopped teaching you anything. What began as a thoughtful pause may have turned into stalling, with decisions put off because making them feels uncomfortable. Watch for sacrifice that has lost its point, too. Giving up your time or your needs can become a role you play, one that quietly asks for credit or keeps you from changing anything. On the other side sits a pull toward the crowd: going along with what everyone else thinks so you do not have to face the question yourself, or guarding your own comfort at someone else's expense. Ask what you are really holding out for. Then either let the thing go or take the next step.","loveUp":"Love asks for patience and a fresh angle. If you are in a relationship, try seeing a recurring disagreement from your partner's point of view before responding. If you are single, a quieter stretch can reveal what you actually want. Not every question needs an answer today. Let things settle, and trust what becomes clear.","loveRev":"Waiting has turned into limbo. You may be giving far more than you receive and calling it devotion, or putting your life on hold for someone who has not made the same choice. Whether single or partnered, notice where you are sacrificing without reason. Your needs count too, and you are free to make a decision of your own.","workUp":"A project or career move may be in a holding pattern, and that can work in your favor. Use the time to reflect, rethink your approach, or look at a problem from an unusual angle. A short-term sacrifice, like extra study or a step sideways, could lead to real insight. Trust your instincts before acting.","workRev":"Delays at work are becoming an excuse. Maybe you keep putting off a decision, or you are taking on extra work nobody asked for and quietly resenting it. Be careful, too, about following office consensus just to avoid standing out. Decide what you actually think, name what you need, and move forward.","picture":"A young man hangs upside down by one foot from a living wooden beam shaped like a T, green leaves sprouting at its ends. His red leggings end in yellow shoes, and his free leg bends behind the other knee, making the shape of a number four. He wears a blue-gray tunic, and his arms are folded out of sight behind his back. His face is calm, not pained, and a golden halo glows around his head against a plain pale background. Hanging this way looks chosen rather than forced, and the light around his head suggests understanding reached by seeing things differently."},
"major-13":{"up":"Something is finishing, and there is no point pretending otherwise. A relationship, a job, a habit, a version of yourself that fit an older season: whatever has run its course is ready to be closed. Endings can be sad, and you are allowed to feel that. You may also be losing a support you have relied on, which can leave you feeling exposed for a while. Yet clearing is what makes room. The space left behind is where something new eventually takes root, often in a shape you could not have planned. Let the change be thorough rather than halfway. Grieve what needs grieving, then turn toward what comes after.","rev":"A chapter has ended, but you are still holding the door shut behind you. Maybe you keep returning to a situation that has clearly run out of life, or you have gone numb and are moving through your days on autopilot. That heavy, sleepy stillness usually means a change is being held back rather than lived through. It can also feel as if a hope has slipped away and nothing has replaced it yet. Be patient with yourself, but be honest too. Nothing new can start while you are guarding the old thing. Take one small step of release, a box packed away, a message you stop rereading, and let some fresh air in.","loveUp":"A relationship pattern is ending, and that is making space. If you are partnered, an old way of relating may be falling away so something more honest can grow between you. If you are single, you may be closing the book on a past connection for good. Let the ending be complete, and stay open to what follows.","loveRev":"You may be holding on to a connection, a hope or an old hurt that has already run its course. Replaying the past keeps your heart busy but not free. Whether you are single or in a relationship, notice where you have gone numb or stuck. Letting go gently gives you room to feel something new.","workUp":"A phase of your working life is wrapping up, perhaps a project, a role or a way of doing things. Resist the urge to patch up what is clearly finished. Tie up loose ends, take what you have learned, and clear the decks. Endings at work often open space for a direction that suits you better.","workRev":"Something at work has lost its spark, yet you keep going through the motions. Clinging to an outdated process or a role you have outgrown can leave you drained. Ask what you are afraid would happen if you let it change. A small move toward renewal, like a new skill or an honest conversation, can break the inertia.","picture":"A skeleton in black armor rides a white horse, a red plume streaming from his helmet and small skulls decorating the bridle. He carries a black banner showing a large white rose. Before him a figure in golden robes and a tall pointed hat stands with hands pressed together, while a young woman and a small child kneel nearby, the woman turning her face away. Another figure lies fallen on the ground. Beyond them a river flows toward the horizon, where a sun shines beside a pale tower. No one stops the rider, yet that distant sun hints the scene is a passage, not the final word."},
"major-14":{"up":"Balance comes from blending, not from choosing one extreme. You are being asked to mix things with care: work and rest, ambition and patience, your needs and someone else's. The right amount of each makes something better than either alone. This is the long middle of a process, where steady, unglamorous effort matters more than big gestures. Pace yourself. Use your time, energy and resources wisely, and meet other people halfway where you can. Small adjustments, repeated often, add up to real steadiness. If you feel pulled to rush, see whether a little more patience would give a better result. Moderation is not dull here. It is a skill, and you are getting good at it.","rev":"The mix is off. Maybe you are pouring too much into one area of life and leaving another dry, or swinging between extremes, all in and then worn out. Impatience may be tempting you to skip the slow part of a process that genuinely needs time. There can also be friction between people or goals that do not blend well: competing interests pulling a plan in different directions, or a partnership where each side wants something the other cannot give. Do not force the combination. Step back and notice what is overflowing and what is running low. Slowing down and adjusting one ingredient at a time brings back the flow.","loveUp":"Harmony grows through patience and compromise. If you are partnered, meeting each other halfway on small things keeps the bond steady and kind. If you are single, a calm, unhurried approach to dating lets real compatibility show itself. Nothing needs to be rushed. The right blend of closeness and space makes love feel easy.","loveRev":"Something in love feels out of balance. One person may be giving much more, or the relationship keeps swinging between intense closeness and distance. If you are single, you might be rushing into connections or holding everyone at arm's length. Look for the middle ground, and remember that a good match needs willingness from both sides.","workUp":"Steady, well-managed effort is your strength at work now. Blend skills from different areas, balance competing demands, and keep your pace sustainable. Careful use of time and resources pays off. You may be the one who helps others find common ground, and your calm approach is likely to be appreciated.","workRev":"Work may be tipping into excess, with too many hours, too many commitments, or projects that pull against each other. Frustration with slow progress could tempt you to cut corners. Look at where priorities clash, simplify what you can, and give the process the time it needs. Balance brings back your effectiveness.","picture":"An angel with deep red wings stands in a white robe, one foot in a pool of water and the other on the stony bank. A golden circle marks the forehead, rays shine around the curly hair, the eyes are lowered, and a small triangle inside a square sits on the chest. The angel pours a stream of water from one golden cup into another, the flow slanting in a way that looks almost impossible. Yellow irises bloom on the right, and on the left a bright sun rises over distant blue mountains. Every detail speaks of careful mixing and calm, steady presence."},
"major-15":{"up":"Something has a strong grip on you right now, and it may feel bigger than your willpower. A habit you keep returning to, a relationship that runs on intensity, a craving for approval, status or control: whatever it is, it pulls with real force. Some of it may even feel fated, and that does not automatically make it wrong. This energy can fuel extraordinary effort, the kind of drive that gets a hard thing done. The trouble starts when desire decides for you. Look honestly at what you feel you cannot live without, and at the loop that keeps bringing you back. Naming the chain is the first step to seeing that it is looser than it feels.","rev":"The chain is starting to show. You may be waking up to a pattern that has run your choices for a while, and seeing it clearly is already a kind of freedom. Now comes the practical part. Old habits often pull harder just as you try to leave them, so expect a few wobbles and do not treat them as proof that you cannot change. Watch, too, for the smaller traps: petty resentments, excuses, the spots you would rather not look at. It is easy to swap one hold for another without noticing. Take the loop apart one link at a time, lean on people who support the new direction, and give yourself credit for every step.","loveUp":"Attraction is strong, possibly stronger than good sense. If you are in a relationship, notice whether passion is bringing you closer or whether jealousy or control has crept in. If you are single, you may feel drawn to someone who is exciting but not good for you. Enjoy desire, but make sure you are choosing it freely.","loveRev":"You may be seeing an unhealthy pattern in love for what it is. Whether it is a cycle of chasing unavailable people or a relationship built on control, recognition is the turning point. Single or partnered, set boundaries that protect your well-being, and let go of what keeps you small. Freedom starts with your own choices.","workUp":"Ambition can drive you to impressive effort, but check whether it is serving you or consuming you. A role that rewards you well but drains you, or a chase for status, may have more hold than you realize. Put limits on the pull of work, and remember that you choose how much of yourself to give.","workRev":"You are starting to see what has kept you stuck at work, whether an overwork habit, a draining dynamic or a fear of leaving your comfort zone. Awareness gives you options. Watch for pettiness and office politics that cloud your judgment. Set clearer boundaries and put your energy into work that feels healthy and meaningful.","picture":"A horned figure with a goat's face and dark bat wings squats on a black pedestal, one hand raised with the palm open and the other holding a flaming torch pointed downward. An upside-down five-pointed star sits above his brow, and his furry legs end in claws. Chained to a ring on the pedestal stand a naked man and woman, each with small horns and a tail, hers ending in a bunch of grapes. The background is solid black. Look closely at the chains: they hang loose around the pair's necks, as if they could lift them off whenever they chose."},
"major-16":{"up":"Something built on a shaky foundation is coming down, and it may happen faster than you expected. A belief, a plan, an arrangement you thought was solid can crack open in a single moment of truth. It is unsettling, and you are allowed to feel shaken. Still, what falls now is what could not hold, and there is relief hidden in that. The shock clears away pretense and shows you what is real. You do not have to rebuild everything today. Let the dust settle, protect what matters most, and pay attention to what the collapse revealed. A stronger structure, one grounded in truth, can be built from here.","rev":"You can feel the cracks, but you are working hard to keep the walls standing. Maybe you sense that a situation cannot last and keep patching it anyway, hoping the shake-up will pass you by. Resisting a change that needs to happen tends to stretch the discomfort out rather than avoid it. There may also be a hemmed-in feeling, as if someone else's rules or pressure are boxing you in, or your own fear is. The upheaval here is milder, but it still asks something of you. Ask what you are protecting and whether it is worth the effort. Letting a weak structure go on your own terms is usually easier than waiting for it to fall.","loveUp":"A sudden truth may shake up your love life. If you are partnered, an honest revelation or unexpected event could disrupt the routine and prompt a real conversation. If you are single, an illusion about what you want may fall away. It is unsettling, but it clears the ground for something more genuine to grow.","loveRev":"You may be avoiding a needed shake-up in love, holding on to something that no longer feels right out of fear of what change would bring. If you are single, you could be stuck in old patterns. Whether partnered or not, gentle honesty now is kinder than waiting for pressure to build. You are allowed to choose change.","workUp":"An unexpected shift at work, such as a restructure, a plan that falls through or a truth coming out, may catch you off guard. Stay steady and adaptable. What collapses now was likely unstable anyway. Use the moment to rethink your direction and build on something more solid and honest.","workRev":"You may sense trouble brewing at work but keep hoping it will fix itself. Or you feel boxed in by rigid control or someone's heavy-handed authority. Delaying hard choices can make the eventual shift bigger. Look at what needs to change, and start adjusting on your own terms while you still have room to move.","picture":"A tall gray tower stands on a jagged rocky peak against a black sky, and a zigzag bolt of lightning strikes its top. The golden crown that capped it is knocked loose and tumbling. Flames burst from its windows, and two figures fall headfirst through the air, one in a red cloak and one wearing a crown. Small yellow flames drift down on both sides among gray clouds. Everything happens at once. The crown being knocked away first suggests that what was placed on top, a pride or an illusion, is the first thing to go."},
"major-17":{"up":"After a hard stretch, something inside you is starting to breathe again. You may have been through a loss or a season of going without, and this is the quiet that comes afterward, when the worst has passed and repair can begin. Hope does not need to be loud. It can be as simple as feeling a little lighter when you wake up, or sensing that the future has room in it again. Take care of yourself gently and let generosity flow both ways, giving and receiving. Trust the small signs of renewal. You do not have to have everything figured out to feel guided. Keep following the light that feels true.","rev":"Hope feels thin right now, and you might be looking away from the very things that could restore it. After a disappointment, it is natural to feel powerless or to stop expecting anything good. Protecting yourself that way can harden into cynicism, or into a proud refusal to accept help. Neither lets the light in. You may also be waiting for a sign before you let yourself believe again. Try the opposite order: take one small step toward what renews you, a walk, a creative hour, an honest chat with a friend, and let the feeling follow. Your capacity for hope has not gone anywhere. It is resting.","loveUp":"Your heart is ready to open again. If you are partnered, a gentle, honest renewal can bring you closer after a difficult time. If you are single, you may feel ready to trust again and to meet people with fresh eyes. Show up as you are, and let genuine connection find you without forcing it.","loveRev":"Past hurt may be making it hard to believe in love. You might be keeping your guard up or assuming the worst about people. If you are single, take small steps back toward connection at your own pace. If you are partnered, share your doubts honestly rather than withdrawing. Hope can be rebuilt slowly.","workUp":"After setbacks, optimism is returning at work. It is a good time to reconnect with the purpose behind what you do, share ideas freely and look toward the long term. Your calm, open approach can inspire others. Small, steady progress builds real confidence in your direction.","workRev":"Discouragement may be dulling your motivation at work. You might feel unseen or doubt your abilities, or you could be brushing off good advice out of pride. Reconnect with what first drew you to your work, ask for support, and set one small, achievable goal to rebuild momentum.","picture":"A woman with golden hair kneels by a still pool under a pale blue-green sky, one knee on the ground and one foot resting on the water. She pours water from two jugs, one back into the pool and one onto the land, where it runs off in small streams. Above her shines a large yellow eight-pointed star circled by seven smaller white stars. On a hill to the right, a small bird perches in a tree, and pink mountains line the far horizon. She is unclothed and unhurried, and the whole scene feels like a deep breath after a storm."},
"major-18":{"up":"Not everything is what it seems right now, and you may be finding it hard to see straight. Fears can grow larger in the dark, and your imagination may be filling gaps with worst-case stories. At the same time, some of the unease is worth listening to. There may be half-truths around you, a rumor, a person who is not being fully honest, or a detail that has been left out. Do not make big decisions from inside the fog. Move slowly, check facts before trusting them, and pay attention to dreams and gut feelings without treating them as proof. Clarity comes gradually. For now, find your footing one step at a time.","rev":"The fog is starting to thin. Something that confused or frightened you is becoming easier to name, and once you can name it, it tends to lose some of its power. You may be catching a small deception, or realizing that an old fear was never as big as it looked. Things may still feel changeable for a while, with moods shifting, plans wobbling, or someone going quiet when you want answers. That is part of the in-between. Resist filling the silence with guesses. Keep asking honest questions, of others and of yourself, and notice how much steadier you feel with each thing you see clearly.","loveUp":"Emotions in love may feel confusing or intense. If you are partnered, unspoken fears or mixed signals could cloud things, so talk openly rather than guessing. If you are single, someone may not be quite what they seem at first. Take your time, trust your instincts, and let the truth show itself.","loveRev":"Confusion in love is beginning to clear. If you are partnered, a misunderstanding can finally be named and worked through. If you are single, you may see a past situation for what it really was. Moods may still shift, so be patient, keep communication honest, and do not fill silences with fears.","workUp":"Things at work may be unclear, with incomplete information, hidden agendas or shifting expectations. Hold off on big commitments until you have the facts. Keep a record of agreements, verify what you hear, and be careful with gossip. Trust your instincts, but let evidence confirm them before you act.","workRev":"Clarity is returning at work. Confusion or a misleading situation is coming to light, and you can start making sense of it. Some instability may remain as things settle, so double-check details and stay flexible. Honest questions will help you get the full picture before moving forward.","picture":"A large yellow disc holding a sleeping crescent face in profile hangs in a blue-green sky, rays spreading around it and yellow drops falling below. Two gray towers stand on either side of the scene. Between them an orange dog and a pale wolf lift their heads and howl upward, and a crayfish crawls out of a pool in the foreground. Beyond the animals, green fields roll toward distant blue mountains. Everything feels half awake. The creatures respond to a light that shows shapes without detail, the way instinct stirs before the mind has words."},
"major-19":{"up":"Warmth and clarity are shining on your life right now. Things that felt complicated become simpler, and the good in front of you is easy to see and enjoy. This is a time for contentment: a comfortable home, laughter with people you love, work that goes well, long days that leave you tired in a good way. Happy partnerships and shared joys are especially favored. There is no hidden catch. Let yourself enjoy what is working without waiting for the other shoe to drop. Confidence comes naturally in this light, and your openness draws others toward you. Celebrate the plain, everyday good things, and share them generously.","rev":"Light is still reaching you, only filtered through a few clouds. Good things are happening, but you may not be feeling them fully, perhaps because you are distracted, tired, or waiting for everything to be perfect before you let yourself be happy. A plan might be running later than you hoped, or the clear answer you want has not quite arrived. None of this cancels the warmth. It just dims it a little. Look for the small joys you have been rushing past and give them your attention. Keep expectations realistic and enjoy what is going well now. Brightness returns more easily when you stop postponing it.","loveUp":"Love feels warm and uncomplicated. If you are in a relationship, you may enjoy a stretch of real happiness, easy affection and shared plans. If you are single, your confidence and openness make you easy to approach. Enjoy connection for what it is, and let joy be the point rather than a prize.","loveRev":"Happiness in love is present but muted. Stress, routine or unmet expectations may be dimming the warmth between you and a partner. If you are single, you might be holding back your true self. Bring some lightness back in, share what you appreciate, and let the good things count.","workUp":"Success and recognition come more easily when you show up as yourself at work. Projects run smoothly, your energy is noticed, and collaboration feels natural. It is a good time to share ideas, take the lead and celebrate what your team accomplishes together. Enjoy the momentum and let it build.","workRev":"Progress at work is real but slower or less visible than you would like. You may be overlooking your wins because you are focused on what is not done. Recognize what is going well, keep expectations grounded, and stay patient. Steady effort is what brings the brightness back.","picture":"A huge golden sun with a calm human face fills the top of the card, sending out rays that alternate between straight and wavy. Below it, a naked child with a wreath of flowers and a red feather in the hair rides a gray-white horse bareback, arms spread wide. A long red banner streams beside them. Behind the child runs a gray stone wall, with tall sunflowers rising over it. The child's open arms suggest a joy with nothing to hide, and the sun seems to be looking on the whole scene with quiet approval."},
"major-20":{"up":"Something is calling you to wake up and answer. It might be a truth you have circled for months, a talent you set aside, or a chance to look at the last chapter of your life honestly and decide what comes next. The invitation is to look back without flinching, keep what was good, forgive what needs forgiving, including your own missteps, and rise into a new position. Most people feel this as a clear inner knowing rather than a dramatic event. You already sense the change being asked of you. Answer it with honesty instead of harshness. A fresh start is available, and it grows out of the review, not in spite of it.","rev":"The call is there, but you may be muffling it. Sometimes that looks like putting off a decision you already know you need to make, hoping more deliberation will spare you the discomfort of choosing. Other times it looks like turning an honest review into a trial where you play both the accused and the harshest critic. Neither helps you move. Timidity keeps you in the old position, and self-blame keeps you replaying the past instead of learning from it. Ask yourself what you would do if you trusted your own judgment a little more and punished yourself a little less. Then take one step that answers the call, even a quiet one.","loveUp":"Honest reflection is changing the way you love. If you are in a relationship, this is a good moment to talk openly about what has worked, what has hurt and what you both want now, then begin again from that truth. If you are single, look back at old patterns with kindness and notice how much you have grown. You are ready for a different kind of connection.","loveRev":"Old regrets may be steering your choices more than you realize. Maybe you keep going over a past relationship, blaming yourself or someone else, or you sense a conversation is overdue and keep delaying it. Whether you are single or partnered, go easier on yourself and be honest about what you need. Clarity comes from listening to yourself, not from replaying the same story.","workUp":"A review of your working life is due, and it could lead to a real change of position. You may be asked to step up, or you may realize a role no longer fits the person you have become. Look at your record honestly, name what you have learned, and respond to the opportunity that feels like a genuine calling rather than an obligation.","workRev":"You might be hesitating on a work decision because you are afraid of getting it wrong, or judging your own performance so harshly that you undersell yourself. Weighing options has its place, but endless weighing becomes its own trap. Gather what you need, give yourself a point at which you will decide, and let your experience have the credit it has earned.","picture":"An angel with red wings and golden, flame-tipped hair leans out of gray clouds, blowing a long golden trumpet. A white banner marked with a red cross hangs from it. Below, pale unclothed figures rise from open coffins floating on gray-green water: a man with his hands lifted, a woman with her arms spread wide, and a child seen from behind reaching upward between them. More figures raise their arms farther back, and white peaks line the horizon. Every one of them is turned toward the sound. The scene suggests an awakening, a summons heard all at once, and the choice to stand up and answer it."},
"major-21":{"up":"A cycle is coming full circle, and you get to feel the satisfaction of having seen it through. Maybe a long project is finished, a stage of life has settled into place, or you finally feel at home in yourself after years of searching. Success here is earned, and it tends to open a wider life: travel, a move, new routes that appear because you are ready for them. Let yourself arrive. Mark the moment, thank the people who walked part of the way with you, and notice how much you now hold together that once felt scattered. Every completion is also a doorway, and you get to step through this one whole.","rev":"You are closer to the finish than it feels, but something keeps the circle from closing. It might be one loose end you keep avoiding, a goodbye you have not said, or a habit of staying where things are familiar because change would ask more of you. Stagnation like this is rarely dramatic. It is the quiet sense of being stuck on the last lap. Look for the small unfinished piece and deal with it directly. Sometimes completion means accepting that good enough is done. Once you release what has been holding you in place, movement returns, and the next chapter can begin on steady footing.","loveUp":"Love feels whole and settled. In a relationship, you may reach a milestone that shows how far you have come together, or simply enjoy the feeling of being truly at home with each other. If you are single, you are coming into your own, and that sense of fullness shows. A new connection could even begin while you are traveling or somewhere unfamiliar.","loveRev":"Something in your love life feels nearly resolved but not quite. Perhaps an old relationship still has an ending you never spoke aloud, or you and a partner keep circling the same issue without closing it. If you are single, check whether you are waiting for a perfect moment to begin. Finish what needs finishing in your own heart, and room opens for what comes next.","workUp":"A major piece of work reaches completion, and your effort is recognized. This is a strong moment to wrap things up well, share the credit and take stock of what you have built. New routes may open, including roles that involve travel, relocation or working with a much wider circle. Step into the next level knowing you have earned it.","workRev":"A project may be stalling just short of the finish line, or you feel stuck in a role that stopped growing some time ago. Look for the loose thread: an approval never requested, a final report never written, a skill you have not claimed. Closing that loop, even imperfectly, restores your momentum and helps you see where you want to go next.","picture":"A dancing figure, wrapped only in a long violet sash, floats inside a tall oval wreath of green leaves bound at top and bottom with red ribbons. She holds a slim white wand in each hand, one leg crossed lightly behind the other as if caught mid-step. The background is a calm pale green. In the four corners, clouds hold a human head, an eagle, a bull and a lion, watching from every side. The wreath frames her like a finished circle, and her easy balance suggests freedom inside wholeness, movement that has found its center."},
"wands-01":{"up":"A spark has caught, and it wants somewhere to go. You may feel a surge of energy around a new idea, a creative impulse you cannot ignore, or the urge to start something that feels entirely yours. Beginnings like this are the source of everything that follows, so trust the rush of enthusiasm while it is strong. You do not need the whole plan, only a first move: the email, the sketch, the phone call, the opening page. Openings that appear now often bring support or resources along with them, so lean toward yes where your gut says yes. Fire grows when it is fed, so give it action before doubt has time to cool it.","rev":"The spark is there, but it is not catching. Maybe you had a strong idea and let it sit until the excitement faded, or you started with a burst of energy and then scattered it across too many things. There can be a clouded kind of joy here, a mix of wanting and frustration, like knowing what you want and not quite reaching it. That is not failure. It is a nudge to ask what is actually in the way: fear, fatigue, or simply poor timing. Pick the one idea that still makes your pulse quicken and give it one small, concrete step. Momentum comes back more easily than you expect.","loveUp":"Attraction and fresh energy are rising. If you are single, a spark with someone new could be exciting, and it is worth seeing where it leads. If you are in a relationship, desire can come back with real warmth, especially if you try something new together or say plainly what excites you. Enjoy the heat and let it grow honestly.","loveRev":"Interest may be flickering without turning into anything real. You might feel drawn to someone but keep holding back, or notice that passion in a relationship has cooled because routine took over. Instead of waiting for the feeling to return on its own, name what you want and make one small, warm gesture. If the spark is shared, it responds to attention.","workUp":"A promising idea or opening is right in front of you. This is a good time to pitch the proposal, begin the side project, or take the first step on something your team has not tried yet. Your enthusiasm is contagious, so use it to rally support. Help and resources tend to follow visible energy, so start before you feel fully ready.","workRev":"An idea at work may be stuck at the planning stage, or your energy is spread across too many beginnings. Delays and false starts can feel discouraging, but they are also information. Narrow your focus to the project that genuinely excites you and set one clear next step. A spark left alone fades, while one you tend keeps building.","picture":"A pale hand reaches out of a gray cloud on the right, gripping a single stout wooden wand, reddish brown and alive with small green shoots. Several leaves have come loose and drift in the air around it, and faint rays of light surround the hand. Below lies a quiet landscape: green hills, a castle perched on a rise to the left, a winding river and a few small trees in front of a band of distant red hills. The wand is held out like a gift, raw potential waiting for someone to take it up and use it."},
"wands-02":{"up":"You have made a start, and now you are standing at the edge of it, deciding how far to go. What you have built so far gives you a solid base, yet part of you looks out and feels restless, aware that there is more world beyond the walls. That mix of satisfaction and longing is useful, because it pushes you to plan. Take time to think about where you really want to take this, what the bigger picture looks like, and which option fits the life you want rather than the one that only looks impressive. Planning now is not stalling. It is the difference between drifting and choosing a direction on purpose.","rev":"A plan has stalled at the edge. You may be caught in endless comparing without ever committing, or feel unexpectedly unsettled by how big the next step looks. Fear of the unknown can dress itself up as caution. Surprises may also shake up your map, bringing a rush of wonder along with a jolt of worry. Notice what you are waiting for. If it is certainty, it may never arrive in full. Choose the option that still feels alive when you picture yourself inside it, and take one practical step toward it. A small commitment is often all it takes to end the hovering and get you moving again.","loveUp":"You may be thinking seriously about where your love life is headed. In a relationship, that could mean talking through shared plans, a move, or the next stage together. If you are single, you are getting clearer about what you want and may feel ready to widen your circle. Look past your usual horizons, and let your choices reflect your real hopes.","loveRev":"Uncertainty about direction may be creating tension. You or a partner might hesitate to take the next step, or one of you feels restless even when things look good from the outside. If you are single, notice whether you are holding back because the unknown feels risky. Talk openly about fears and hopes, and let everyone involved answer freely.","workUp":"You are in a strong position to plan your next move at work. Consider growing your role, reaching into new territory, or sketching out a longer-range strategy. Research your options carefully and weigh your ambitions against what actually satisfies you. Bold thinking works best when it rests on the ground you have already secured.","workRev":"Career plans may feel stuck, either because you are overanalyzing or because a surprise has thrown off your timeline. The comfort of familiar ground can keep you rooted longer than you meant to stay. Revisit your goals, simplify the plan, and pick one concrete step. Progress comes from moving, even slowly, rather than waiting for a perfect picture.","picture":"A man in a red cap and a long red cloak stands on the battlement of a stone wall, his back half turned to us. One hand holds a small globe, and the other grips a tall wand, while a second wand is fixed to the wall beside him with a metal ring. He gazes out over a bay, green fields, distant mountains and a small house with a red roof. On the wall to the left, a panel shows white lilies and red roses crossed over each other. He looks secure at home, yet he is weighing the whole wide world in his hand."},
"wands-03":{"up":"The hard part is behind you, and now you are watching for results. You have made your plans, taken your risks and sent your efforts out into the world, and this is the stretch where you wait to see what comes back. It can feel exciting and a little nerve-racking at the same time. Keep your gaze on the long view, because more options are opening than you can see from close up. Help may also come from someone who wants your venture to succeed, so stay open to working together. Be patient but alert, ready to respond when news or an opportunity finally sails into view.","rev":"The wait is running longer than you hoped, and you may be tempted to stare at the horizon instead of tending what is in front of you. Some delays come from outside, but others come from planning so far ahead that the next small step gets missed. There is good news here too: a stretch of struggle may be easing, even if full relief has not arrived yet. Bring your attention back to the present. Check which plans still make sense, adjust your expectations, and keep doing the practical work. Troubles tend to lift faster when you stop holding your breath for them to end.","loveUp":"Your love life is widening. If you are in a relationship, you may be making shared plans, including travel or bigger dreams you build together. If you are single, your openness to new people and places could lead to interesting connections, perhaps with someone from a very different background. Trust that the time and care you have put in are growing into something.","loveRev":"Frustration can build when a relationship is not moving as quickly as you hoped, or when distance, literal or emotional, keeps getting in the way. If you are single, you might be picturing a far-off ideal and overlooking good people close by. Ease up on the long-range forecasting and pay attention to what is real and present now.","workUp":"Your efforts are starting to pay off, and new possibilities are showing up on the horizon. This is a good time for collaboration, reaching out to partners or clients who can help carry your work further. Keep the bigger picture in view and trust that your groundwork was solid. Wider audiences, new teams or projects abroad may be within reach.","workRev":"Delays or unmet expectations may leave you impatient at work. Plans that looked promising might need more time or a different approach. Instead of fixating on distant outcomes, focus on the steps you can control today. Difficulties are likely easing, and steady attention to the tasks in front of you keeps things moving in the right direction.","picture":"A figure stands with his back to us on a green and rocky rise, one hand resting on a tall wand while two more stand planted beside him. He wears a long red robe with a green cloak over one shoulder and a black and gold checked band across his back, and a white band circles his dark hair. Below him stretches a wide golden sea, with a few small ships sailing toward distant hills under a pale yellow sky. He watches calmly and patiently, as though waiting for something he sent out to come home."},
"wands-04":{"up":"Something good has come together, and it deserves to be celebrated. This is a time of welcome and stability: a home that feels right, a gathering of people you love, a milestone reached, a stretch of peace after effort. The foundation you built is holding. Let yourself enjoy it instead of rushing on to the next thing. Invite others in, mark the occasion, and notice the sense of belonging around you. Good fortune may arrive unexpectedly now, often in simple forms like a warm welcome or a shared meal. Harmony like this is not an accident. It is the fruit of work you have done, so take the pause.","rev":"The good things are still here, but the celebration may be on hold. Plans for a gathering might shift, a milestone could arrive later than expected, or you may be too busy or distracted to enjoy what you have built. Sometimes a little tension at home or among friends makes it hard to relax into the moment. None of that erases the underlying goodness. Warmth and steady growth remain available, just delayed or unnoticed. Slow down enough to appreciate what is working, and reach out to the people who matter, even in small ways. The party is postponed, not canceled, and your sense of home comes back with a little attention.","loveUp":"Relationships feel secure and joyful. If you are partnered, you may celebrate a milestone, set up a home together, or simply enjoy a season of closeness and ease. If you are single, you may feel content with your life and open to someone who fits naturally into your circle. Enjoy the happiness around you and share it generously.","loveRev":"Plans for togetherness may be on hold, or small tensions might be keeping you from fully enjoying each other. If you are single, you might feel out of step with friends who are pairing off, even though you have plenty of love around you. Focus on what is already good. The warmth is still present, waiting for your attention.","workUp":"You have reached a milestone at work, and it is worth marking. Team spirit is strong, projects are coming together, and a sense of stability supports you. Celebrate the progress with colleagues, recognize the shared effort, and let yourself feel settled for a while. A pleasant surprise may come your way, so stay open to recognition.","workRev":"Recognition or a planned celebration at work may be postponed, or you might feel less settled than you expected to. The foundations are still sound, so avoid assuming the worst. Take time to appreciate your team and your own progress, and look for small ways to build a sense of belonging while the bigger moment waits.","picture":"Four tall wands stand in the foreground, with a garland of roses, greenery and fruit strung between their tops and tied with red ribbons. Beyond them two figures lift bouquets high over their heads, one in a pale blue robe and one in red. Behind them rises a gray castle wall with a round tower capped by a red roof, more small figures gather near the wall on the left, and a little bridge arches on the right. The bright yellow sky gives the whole scene a festive warmth, like a homecoming or a harvest celebration."},
"wands-05":{"up":"Competition and friction are in the air, but not all of it is serious. You may be in a lively disagreement, a crowded field of ideas, or a situation where everyone wants to be heard at once. Much of this is practice: people testing their strength, trying out positions and pushing each other to do better. Treat it as useful noise rather than a real battle. Speak up, contribute your view, and learn from the pushback. The scramble to get ahead can sharpen your skills if you stay fair and keep your sense of humor. A little chaos now can clear the way for something stronger later.","rev":"Tension is either being avoided or boiling over. You might be keeping the peace so carefully that important disagreements never get said, or you might be caught in arguments that have turned personal and draining. Petty disputes, contradictions and games of one-upmanship can eat a lot of energy. Look at what the conflict is really about. Sometimes a direct, calm conversation clears the air better than weeks of tiptoeing. Other times the wiser move is to step back and let things cool. Either way, a disagreement can work in your favor when you handle it with honesty and respect.","loveUp":"Lively energy can stir up friction in love. Couples may bicker about small things, but honest debate can lead to better understanding and even more spark. If you are single, dating might feel competitive or chaotic for a while. Keep a light touch, say what you need clearly, and remember that disagreement does not have to mean you are incompatible.","loveRev":"You may be avoiding conflict to keep the peace, or small irritations are growing into bigger arguments. Neither helps. Whether you are single or in a relationship, look for the root of the tension and speak about it calmly. Clear boundaries and fair, respectful discussion can turn friction into growth instead of resentment.","workUp":"Competition at work is heating up, whether with rivals, colleagues or clashing ideas in a meeting. Use it to sharpen your skills and test your thinking against others. Brainstorming may be noisy, but noise is often where breakthroughs start. Stay focused on the goal rather than winning every argument, and treat challengers as sparring partners.","workRev":"Workplace friction may be wearing you down, whether through ongoing disputes, office politics or a conflict nobody wants to name. Look for ways to clarify roles and expectations. A calm, direct conversation can settle more than you expect. If you have been avoiding a disagreement, this is a good time to speak up respectfully.","picture":"Five young men crowd together on uneven ground, each raising a long wooden wand, and the wands cross and clash in a tangled knot above their heads. Their clothes are all different: yellow, red, dark green, black, and one white tunic dotted with green spots. Some brace their feet while others swing high, yet no one seems to land a blow. The pale blue-green sky gives the scene an open, almost playful air. It looks more like a rough practice match than a real fight, with energy spilling out in every direction."},
"wands-06":{"up":"Your efforts are being seen, and it feels good to be recognized. This may be a public win, praise from someone whose opinion matters, good news you have been hoping for, or simply the quiet confidence of knowing you did well. Let yourself receive it. Success here is shared: others helped you get this far, and they are cheering you on. The moment invites you to enjoy the victory without letting it go to your head. A hope you have carried for a while is finally being answered. Use the momentum to lift others, and carry this confidence into your next challenge with grace and gratitude.","rev":"Recognition may feel delayed, or the praise you receive does not match what you hoped for. You might worry about losing your standing, or sense that the support around you is not entirely sincere. Sometimes the fear is louder than the facts. Look closely before assuming anyone is against you, and notice whether you rely too much on outside approval. Success that depends on applause can feel fragile. Build your confidence from within, recognize your own progress, and stay true to your values. A hope that has been put off can still come through, often later and in a quieter form than you pictured.","loveUp":"Love brings pride and happiness now. If you are in a relationship, you may feel admired and truly valued, and it is a good time to celebrate how far you have come together. If you are single, your confidence is showing, and people notice when you are comfortable in your own skin. Enjoy being seen, and offer the same appreciation in return.","loveRev":"You may feel overlooked or unsure where you stand. In a relationship, needing constant reassurance can create strain, so talk honestly about what makes you feel valued. If you are single, remember that your worth does not depend on being chosen. Build confidence from within, and let the people who appreciate you as you are find their way in.","workUp":"Recognition is within reach at work. A project you led may earn real praise, or your leadership becomes visible to people who had not noticed it before. Share the credit with those who helped, and use the goodwill to strengthen your working relationships. Accept the compliment gracefully instead of brushing it off, and let it fuel the next goal.","workRev":"You may feel your work is not being appreciated, or that credit is going to someone else. Doubts about your standing can chip away at your confidence. Keep doing good work and keep a simple record of what you have contributed. Check whether you depend too much on outside approval, and build your reputation steadily, even if the reward seems slow to arrive.","picture":"A rider crowned with a laurel wreath sits on a white horse, holding a tall wand topped with another laurel wreath tied with a red ribbon. He wears a long dark red cloak over orange clothing. The horse is draped in a green cloth that falls almost to the ground, with a red checked band across its chest. Around them, people on foot carry five more wands, their heads crowded together at the left edge. The pale sky and the raised wreath make the scene feel like a victory parade, a moment of public praise."},
"wands-07":{"up":"You are holding your ground, and you have more strength than you realize. People may challenge your ideas, competitors may crowd in, or you may need to defend a boundary that matters to you. The good news is that you have the higher position: you know your territory, and you have real reasons to stand firm. This is not about aggression. It is about courage, conviction and refusing to give up what you have worked for. Speak clearly, prepare your arguments, and stay steady even when you feel outnumbered. Persistence wins out here, as long as you choose battles that are genuinely worth fighting.","rev":"Defending your position may be wearing you out. Constant challenges, criticism or competition can leave you tired and unsure whether it is worth continuing. You might feel embarrassed, anxious or pulled between different demands. Indecision makes it worse, because a half-hearted defense only invites more pushback. Ask yourself what truly deserves your protection and what you can let go. Sometimes the strongest move is to set down a fight that no longer matters and put your energy where it counts. Rest, regroup, and decide clearly. You do not have to hold every line at once, and choosing your ground is its own kind of courage.","loveUp":"You may need to stand up for your relationship or for your own needs within it. Couples might face outside pressure or strong opinions from friends or family, and staying united helps. If you are single, hold to your standards rather than settling for less than you want. Protecting what you value in love is an act of self-respect.","loveRev":"Constant defending may be draining your love life. You might feel you always have to justify yourself, or you might be guarding your heart so tightly that closeness becomes hard. Whether you are single or partnered, ask what really needs protecting. Letting your guard down, safely and gradually, can open space for real connection.","workUp":"Challenges at work call for confidence. You may need to defend your ideas, negotiate firmly, or protect your position when others push in. Your experience gives you an advantage, so stand firm and prepare well. Persistence and clarity will help you come out ahead, especially if you keep your attention on what really matters.","workRev":"Pushback at work may be leaving you drained or uncertain. You might feel outnumbered or unsure how to answer constant challenges. Decide which issues deserve your energy and let the minor ones go. Clarify your priorities, look for allies, and stop second-guessing yourself. A firm decision reduces the strain and helps you find your footing again.","picture":"A young man in a green tunic and orange hose stands on a rocky rise, gripping one wand diagonally across his body with both hands. Six more wands rise toward him from below, as if held by people we cannot see who are pressing in. His face is tense and his stance wide, ready to push back. Look closely at his feet: he wears a low shoe on one and a boot on the other, as if he dressed in a hurry. The open sky leaves him exposed, but the higher ground gives him the advantage."},
"wands-08":{"up":"Things are moving fast, and you can feel the momentum. Messages arrive, plans suddenly come together, and delays that held you back begin to clear. This is a time for action and quick decisions, when news or opportunities may come in rapid succession. Stay ready to respond, and trust that the energy is heading toward a hopeful outcome. A trip, a burst of fresh communication or a sudden leap of progress are all possible. Keep your aim clear so the speed does not scatter you. When everything is in flight, the best thing you can do is choose your direction and move with confidence.","rev":"Momentum has slowed, or messages are getting crossed. Plans may stall, communication might break down, or you feel frustrated by delays you cannot control. Sometimes the tension turns inward, showing up as restlessness, second-guessing or a nagging conscience about something left unsaid. Arguments can flare when people are impatient, especially at home. Rather than forcing things, check your assumptions and say what you really mean. Rushing now tends to create more confusion. Patience, careful wording and a little quiet reflection will help the energy start moving again, and when the path clears you will be ready to go.","loveUp":"Love moves quickly now. A flirtation turns into long late-night texts, or a relationship suddenly deepens after a slow patch. If you are single, attraction may strike fast, so notice who lights you up in conversation. If you are partnered, it may feel easy to talk and to want each other again. Enjoy the rush, and check in so you both keep pace.","loveRev":"Mixed signals, jealousy or crossed wires may be complicating your love life. Messages might go unanswered or be misread, creating tension or insecurity. Whether you are single or in a relationship, slow down and communicate directly instead of guessing. A calm, honest conversation can clear up misunderstandings, and patience helps you see where things truly stand.","workUp":"Work picks up speed. The reply you were waiting on lands, a stalled project suddenly gets the green light, or several requests arrive at once. Keep your priorities in order so you can respond quickly without dropping anything. Short trips or fast-moving conversations may play a part. Ride the momentum while it is strong, and follow through before it cools.","workRev":"Delays, miscommunication or conflicting messages may be slowing you down. An email gets misread, a decision bounces between people, or a plan changes after you already acted on it. Double-check details before you send them, ask the clarifying question, and avoid reacting in haste. The slowdown is temporary, and careful communication gets things moving again.","picture":"Eight long wooden wands fly through a pale blue-green sky, all parallel, slanting downward from left to right as if thrown in a single motion. Small green leaves sprout along each one. There are no people anywhere. Below, a peaceful countryside stretches out, with green hills, a winding river and a small white house on a hilltop to the left. The empty sky and the matching angle of every wand give a sense of pure motion, something already in flight and about to land."},
"wands-09":{"up":"You have been through a lot to get here, and you are still on your feet. That counts for more than you might think. Maybe it is a long project, a family situation, or a stretch where one problem followed another, and now you are bracing for the next one. Your resilience is real, and so is your fatigue. The message is to hold your ground a little longer, because you are closer to the end than it feels. Delays and pauses may test your patience, but they are not defeat. Protect what you have built, set firm limits where people keep pushing, and let yourself rest in small ways while you finish.","rev":"Your guard has been up for so long that it may have stopped being useful. When every request feels like an attack and every kind word seems suspicious, you end up defending against things that are not actually there. That wears you down faster than the original struggle ever did. It is also possible the obstacles are real but you are trying to face them entirely alone. Look honestly at what still needs protecting and what is just old habit. You might lower the wall a little, accept help from someone who has earned it, or step back and rest before you push on. Strength does not have to mean never setting anything down.","loveUp":"Past hurts may have made you careful, and that care has kept you safe. If you are single, you can keep your standards and still leave the door open a crack. If you are in a relationship, you two may be weathering a hard stretch together. Staying steady and honest now builds trust that lasts.","loveRev":"Old wounds might be doing the talking. You could be reading a partner's small mistakes as proof of the worst, or keeping new people at arm's length before they have a chance. Notice where fear is steering you. Letting someone see that you are tired is not weakness, and it gives them a way in.","workUp":"Work may feel like one push after another, and you have kept going anyway. Hold your position on what matters, whether that is a deadline, a standard or a boundary around your time. Expect a pause or two before things settle. Pace yourself so you still have energy for the final stretch.","workRev":"Defensiveness at work can make ordinary feedback feel like a threat. Ask whether the pressure you are guarding against is still real, or whether you are fighting last year's battle. If the load truly is too heavy, say so plainly and ask for backup. Asking for support is part of doing the job well.","picture":"A man in a red tunic grips a tall wand with both hands and leans into it as though it were holding him up. A white bandage wraps his head, and his eyes slide sideways, watchful. Behind him eight more wands stand upright in a row like a fence, each sprouting small green leaves. Low hills sit on the horizon under a pale green sky, and his yellow boots are planted firmly on flat ground. The bandage says he has already taken some hits, and the careful sideways look says he expects more, yet he has not left his post."},
"wands-10":{"up":"You are carrying more than one person should, and part of you has stopped noticing how heavy it is. Often this comes from success: you said yes, things grew, and now every responsibility seems to land on you. The work may be meaningful, yet the weight is starting to crowd out everything else, including your view of where you are going. Look at the pile honestly. Which pieces are truly yours, and which did you pick up out of habit, guilt or a fear that no one else would do them right? You are near the finish, so the effort has not been wasted. Deciding what to share or drop is how you arrive with something left.","rev":"Relief is possible, and it starts with admitting the load is too much. You might already be setting some of it down, handing off a task, saying no, or letting go of a role that no longer fits. That can feel strange at first, even like failure, but it is the opposite. There may also be tangled situations around you, mixed messages or people quietly pushing their share onto you, and those are worth naming. The other risk is holding on until you drop everything at once, which helps no one. Lighten the bundle deliberately, one piece at a time, and you will start to see the road ahead again.","loveUp":"One person may be doing most of the carrying in your love life, whether that is emotional labor, planning or keeping the peace. If you are partnered, talk about how the weight is shared. If you are single, notice whether a packed schedule or old responsibilities leave any room for someone new. Love needs space to breathe.","loveRev":"You may be ready to put down a burden that has been weighing on your heart, such as an old grudge, a role you took on for someone else, or the belief that you must hold everything together. Set it down. Whether you are dating or committed, lighter shoulders make you easier to reach.","workUp":"Your workload has grown heavier than is sustainable, often because you are good at what you do and people keep handing you more. Finish what is truly yours, then look hard at the rest. Delegating, renegotiating deadlines, or asking which tasks actually matter are signs of good judgment, not weakness.","workRev":"Something at work can shift in your favor if you allow it: a chance to hand off a project, trim your list, or clarify who owns what. Watch for office politics or unclear roles that leave extra work on your desk. Speak up early, before resentment builds, and keep your requests specific.","picture":"A figure in a red tunic hunches forward, arms wrapped around a bundle of ten tall wands. The staves are gathered in front of his face, so his head is buried among them and he cannot see the path. His legs strain as he steps along flat ground. On the right, beyond a few trees, stands a house with a red roof, the place he seems to be heading. Small leaves sprout from the tops of the wands against a pale green sky. Home is close, but the way he holds his load keeps him from seeing it."},
"wands-11":{"up":"A spark of curiosity has caught, and it wants your attention. It might be a new hobby, a place you want to see, a class, or an idea you cannot stop talking about. The feeling is fresh and a little restless, more about exploring than committing, and that is fine for now. Good news or an encouraging message could also arrive, the kind that nudges you to try. As a person, this can be an eager, loyal young spirit in your life who brings energy and speaks well of you. As a role, it is you being the enthusiastic beginner. Follow the thread, ask questions, and see where it leads.","rev":"The excitement is there, but it keeps fizzling before it turns into anything. You might start projects with a rush and drop them a week later, or wait on news that arrives late, garbled or less promising than you hoped. Indecision could have you bouncing between ideas without landing on one. If this points to someone in your life, they may be charming and full of plans, yet unreliable about following through. If it points to you, ask what makes your interest fade so quickly. Sometimes the answer is fear of being bad at something new. Pick one small spark and tend it long enough to see if it can catch.","loveUp":"A playful, flirtatious energy is in the air. If you are single, a new crush or a fun message could brighten things up, so let yourself enjoy it without racing ahead. If you are partnered, bring curiosity back: ask questions you have never asked, plan something new, and treat each other like someone worth getting to know.","loveRev":"Mixed signals or messages that go nowhere may be frustrating you. Someone's enthusiasm might not be matched by follow-through, or you may be the one blowing hot and cold. Whether you are dating or together, say plainly what you want and pay attention to what people do, not just what they text.","workUp":"A new interest at work is worth exploring, maybe a skill, a side project or a role you would like to learn about. News about an opportunity could show up. You do not need to be an expert yet. Volunteer, ask to shadow someone, and let your enthusiasm open doors.","workRev":"Ideas are plentiful but nothing is getting finished, or a hoped-for message is delayed. Scattered focus can make you look less committed than you are. Choose one priority, set a small deadline, and see it through. If you are waiting on news, follow up once, politely, and keep working in the meantime.","picture":"A young man in a feathered cap stands in profile, holding a tall wand upright with both hands and gazing up at its top, where fresh leaves are sprouting. His yellow tunic is covered in black curling shapes, and a tan cloak with a red lining hangs from his shoulders. He wears orange leggings and yellow boots. Around him stretches bare orange ground, with three pointed hills behind. The sky is pale and open. He looks less like someone on his way somewhere than someone wondering what this new thing in his hands could become."},
"wands-12":{"up":"Things are moving fast, and you may be moving with them. A burst of energy, a sudden plan, a trip or even a change of address could be on the horizon. There is courage here, plus a lot of heat and not much patience. That combination gets things started brilliantly and can burn through them just as quickly. As a person, this is someone bold, charming and restless, great company but rarely still for long. As a role, it is you charging after what you want. Enjoy the momentum. Before you leave, though, make sure you know why you are going and what you will need when you get there.","rev":"The energy is there, but it keeps misfiring. You could be rushing into decisions, starting arguments you did not mean to start, or moving so fast that plans break apart halfway. Delays and interruptions might be frustrating you, which only makes you more impatient. If this is someone in your life, they may be exciting but careless with other people's time and feelings. If it is you, slow down enough to aim. Frustration is often a sign that your drive needs a direction, not more speed. Pick one goal, cool your temper before important conversations, and let a plan catch up with your enthusiasm.","loveUp":"Attraction arrives quickly and burns bright. If you are single, someone adventurous may sweep into your life, or you may feel bold enough to make the first move. If you are partnered, a spontaneous trip or a shared adventure can reignite things. Enjoy the rush, and let trust keep pace with it.","loveRev":"Passion without patience can cause friction. Arguments might flare fast, or a connection may feel exciting one week and absent the next. Whether you are single or in a relationship, notice whether you are chasing intensity rather than closeness. Someone who keeps disappearing is showing you something. Respect that, and respect your own need for steadiness.","workUp":"You have drive and the confidence to act, which is useful when a project needs someone to get it moving. A move, travel for work, or a fast-changing assignment could be part of the picture. Channel the energy well: confirm the details, bring others along, and finish the first push before you chase the next idea.","workRev":"Impatience may be costing you at work. Missed details, abandoned projects or a sharp word in a meeting can undo good momentum. Delays might also be stalling a plan you care about. Instead of pushing harder, step back and check your route. A clear plan will get you further than raw speed.","picture":"A knight in silver armor rides a rearing orange horse, one hand raising a leafy wand high and the other gripping the reins. Red plumes stream from his helmet and his arms like flames. Over the armor he wears a yellow tunic patterned with black salamander shapes. Behind him, three pointed orange hills rise from a sandy plain. The horse's front legs are lifted off the ground, and its mane is a tangle of red. Everything in the picture leans forward, suggesting speed, daring and a mind already halfway to the next place."},
"wands-13":{"up":"Confidence and warmth are working together in your favor. You know who you are, and that steady self-assurance draws people in without you having to push. There is generosity here, a big heart paired with a strong spine, and a talent for making things happen, whether that means running a household, a team or a small business. As a person, she may be a friendly, capable woman who has your back and speaks up for you. As a role, it is you stepping into your own charisma. Take up space. Say what you want clearly, share your enthusiasm freely, and let your good results speak for themselves.","rev":"Behind a confident front, doubt may be creeping in. You might be doing everything for everyone, reliably and well, while quietly wondering whether you are enough. That strain can show up as prickliness, comparison or a flash of jealousy you do not like in yourself. If this points to someone around you, they may mean well but be stretched too thin to follow through, or they might be guarded and competitive. If it points to you, look at where you have given your warmth away and kept none for yourself. Reclaim a little time and attention for your own goals. Your spark has not gone out. It needs fuel.","loveUp":"Your warmth and confidence are magnetic right now. If you are single, you may attract admirers simply by being yourself, and you can afford to be direct about what you want. If you are partnered, bring your full, lively self to the relationship and let your affection show. Loyalty and passion sit comfortably together here.","loveRev":"Insecurity or jealousy could be coloring how you see things. You may be comparing yourself to someone else, or caring for a partner so much that your own needs disappear. Whether you are single or attached, rebuild your confidence on your own terms. Love feels steadier when you are not auditioning for it.","workUp":"Your leadership and people skills are strong assets. You can handle a lot at once and still keep morale up, which others notice. This is a good time to take ownership of a project, pitch your idea or show what you can do. Your practical, warm approach can bring real success.","workRev":"You may be spread thin, saying yes to everything and getting little credit for it. Competition or friction with a colleague could also be draining you. Step back, protect your time, and focus on the work that shows your strengths. Goodwill is valuable, but it needs a real chance to be used well.","picture":"A queen in a leafy crown sits squarely on her throne, facing us, a tall sprouting wand in one hand and a sunflower in the other. Her yellow gown falls in heavy folds beneath a grey cloak. The tall back of the throne is red and decorated with rearing lions and sunflowers, and carved lion heads form its arms. At her feet sits a black cat, looking straight out. Pale hills lie behind her under a soft green sky. She is open, rooted and at ease, and the cat hints at a quiet, private side beneath the sunny welcome."},
"wands-14":{"up":"A clear vision and the courage to act on it are available to you. This is leadership that comes from honesty and conviction rather than force, the kind that makes people want to follow. You can see the bigger picture and you are willing to take responsibility for it. As a person, he may be a mature, straightforward man who is generous with advice and keeps his word. As a role, it is you stepping up to guide, decide and set the tone. Trust your experience. Share your plan openly, hold yourself to the standard you expect from others, and let your integrity be the thing people remember.","rev":"Strong leadership can harden into control. You might be pushing your plan on others without really listening, or holding everyone, including yourself, to standards so strict that no one can relax. If this points to someone in your life, they may be fair at heart but severe in how they show it, and their advice could still be worth hearing even if the delivery stings. If it points to you, notice where impatience has replaced vision. Good leaders adapt. Invite input, loosen your grip on the details, and remember that people commit more fully to goals they helped shape.","loveUp":"Steady, honest affection is highlighted. If you are in a relationship, the mood supports commitment, loyalty and a partner who shows up. If you are single, you may be drawn to someone confident and dependable, or you may be ready to lead with your own intentions. Say what you want and mean it.","loveRev":"Someone may be trying to steer the relationship without asking the other person. If that is you, soften your grip and listen. If it is a partner or a date, notice whether their strength feels protective or controlling. Whether you are single or committed, respect runs both ways, and good intentions still need gentle delivery.","workUp":"You are in a strong position to lead, whether or not you have the title. Share your vision, make decisions with integrity, and back your team in public. An experienced mentor could offer guidance worth taking. Your honesty and willingness to take responsibility are what earn trust and move the work forward.","workRev":"A heavy-handed approach may be creating resistance. You or someone above you could be demanding too much, too fast, or refusing to hear other views. Tough standards can help, but they work best alongside fairness and flexibility. Ask for feedback, delegate real authority, and pay attention to advice even when it comes bluntly.","picture":"A king in a long red robe sits in profile on his throne, looking off to the left, a tall leafy wand held upright in his right hand. A green cape covers his shoulders, and a gold crown with sharp points sits on his head. The throne back is yellow and painted with black lions and salamanders, and a patterned cloak spills over the seat. On the ground near his feet crawls a small black salamander. The sky is pale. He sits alert, as if already weighing his next move, and the fiery creatures around him hint at restless energy under calm command."},
"cups-01":{"up":"Your heart is opening, and something good is being offered to it. That might be a new love, a deep friendship, a creative idea, or simply a feeling of contentment you have not had in a while. The emotional tank is filling up, and there is enough to share. Say yes to what nourishes you: kindness, beauty, rest, connection. Let people care for you, and let yourself care back without keeping score. What is arriving is a beginning rather than a finished story, so tend it gently. The more openly you receive what is offered, the more it tends to overflow into the rest of your life.","rev":"Feelings are there, but something is holding them back. You might be keeping your heart closed out of caution, or offering affection that does not quite match what you feel inside. Moods may shift quickly, and an emotional situation that seemed settled could suddenly change shape. None of this means the well has run dry. It points to a blockage worth looking at gently. Ask yourself what you are afraid would happen if you let yourself feel fully, or if you let someone see you. Small steps help: an honest conversation, time alone to process, or simply allowing yourself to name what you want.","loveUp":"Love is flowing freely. If you are single, you may meet someone who feels like a breath of fresh air, or you may simply feel more open to connection. If you are in a relationship, expect renewed tenderness and a chance to deepen things. Be generous with affection and receive it gracefully.","loveRev":"Something may be blocking the flow of feeling. Perhaps you are guarding your heart after a disappointment, or saying the right things without fully meaning them. Whether you are dating or partnered, be honest about where you really stand. Emotional openness begins with you, and it cannot be forced from anyone else.","workUp":"A fulfilling opportunity or a creative idea could appear, the kind of work that feels meaningful and not just necessary. Good relationships with colleagues may grow too. Follow what genuinely interests you and bring heart to your tasks. Enjoying the work is a good sign that you are on the right track.","workRev":"Work may feel emotionally flat right now, or a promising opening could shift unexpectedly. You might be holding back ideas or feelings because the atmosphere does not feel safe. Look for one place where you can contribute something you care about, and pay attention to what drains you versus what refills you.","picture":"A hand reaches out of a curling white cloud, holding a golden cup on its open palm. From above, a white dove dives straight down, carrying a small white wafer marked with a cross toward the cup. An upside-down letter M is marked on the cup's bowl. Streams of water pour over its rim into a pond below, where lily pads float and pink water lilies bloom, while loose drops scatter through the air. The background is a pale, plain cream. The overflowing cup suggests a love or blessing too full to keep to yourself."},
"cups-02":{"up":"Two people are meeting each other halfway, and the connection feels mutual. It could be a romance, a close friendship, a business partnership or a reconciliation, anywhere respect and affection flow in both directions. There is attraction and warmth here, but also balance: each person gives and each receives. Agreements made in good faith do well now, and so do relationships where you feel truly seen. If a bond is forming, nurture it with honesty and small, consistent gestures. If you have been at odds with someone, a chance to find common ground may be opening. Look for the places where your values and theirs already meet.","rev":"The give and take has slipped out of balance. One person may be doing most of the reaching, texting, planning or apologizing, while the other hangs back. Sometimes a misunderstanding is the root, and sometimes it is simply a difference in how much each person wants. Strong feelings can also run ahead of trust, pulling you toward someone faster than the relationship can hold. None of this has to be permanent. Say plainly what you need, then notice how the other person responds of their own free will. A partnership, romantic or otherwise, works when both people choose to show up, not when one carries it alone.","loveUp":"Mutual attraction and respect are highlighted. If you are single, a connection with someone who matches your interest could take shape, especially if you are open and direct. If you are in a relationship, it is a good time to reconnect, talk about shared plans and enjoy the simple pleasure of being on the same team.","loveRev":"An imbalance may be surfacing. You could be putting in far more effort than you receive, or feel distance creeping in. If you are single, notice whether you keep pursuing people who are less interested than you are. Whether you are with someone or not, you deserve affection that is freely returned, and so does everyone else.","workUp":"Partnerships and collaborations are favored. A colleague, client or collaborator could turn out to be an excellent fit, and agreements made now can work well for both sides. Put your energy into working relationships that feel respectful and honest. Mutual trust will make shared goals far easier to reach.","workRev":"A working relationship may feel lopsided, with one person carrying more of the load or getting less of the credit. Communication might have broken down too. Raise the issue calmly and specifically before resentment grows. Clear roles and honest check-ins can rebalance a partnership that is worth keeping.","picture":"A young woman and a young man face each other, each holding out a golden cup. She wears a long white gown, a dark mantle and a laurel wreath. He wears a patterned yellow tunic and a crown of red flowers, and he reaches toward her cup as if to meet it. Between them rises a staff wound with two serpents, topped by a winged red lion's head. Behind them, green hills and a red-roofed house sit under a pale sky. The mirrored pose shows two equals choosing each other, blessed by something larger than both."},
"cups-03":{"up":"Good company and good news belong together here. It is a time to celebrate with people who genuinely care about you, whether that is a reunion, a birthday, or just an evening of laughter with friends. Something may be coming to a happy conclusion, and there is relief in sharing it. Community is the real gift, the friends and chosen family who lift you up and cheer you on. If you have been keeping to yourself, reach out. If you have been going it alone on a project, bring others in. Joy grows when it is shared, and so does comfort in harder seasons. Raise a glass to how far you have come.","rev":"The party is going on, but you may not feel part of it. A crowded social calendar can hide a lack of real closeness, and you might be surrounded by people while still feeling unseen. Overindulgence could also be creeping in: too many late nights, too much of a good thing, fun that leaves you drained instead of refreshed. Sometimes gossip or a third person is unsettling a close circle. A lively season may also be winding down, which is not a bad thing. Notice which relationships truly feed you. Spend more time with those people, fewer hours on obligations that feel hollow, and let yourself celebrate in a quieter way.","loveUp":"Love feels festive and well supported. If you are single, friends may introduce you to someone, or a social event could spark a connection. If you are in a relationship, celebrate together and share your happiness with the people around you. Being loved by your community strengthens the bond you have at home.","loveRev":"Too many outside voices may be crowding your love life, whether that is friends' opinions, gossip, or a third person who creates tension. If you are single, you might be socializing a lot without feeling any real spark. Whether you are dating or together, protect time for genuine one-on-one closeness.","workUp":"Team success is highlighted. A project may wrap up well, and there is reason to celebrate with the people who made it happen. Collaboration, networking and shared credit all serve you now. Thank your colleagues, enjoy the win, and notice how much easier the work feels with good people beside you.","workRev":"Office socializing may be taking up more energy than the work itself, or cliques and gossip could be souring the team. Keep your focus on what you are there to do, and stay kind without getting drawn into drama. If a project is ending, close it out cleanly before moving on.","picture":"Three women stand close together in a circle, each lifting a golden cup high as if in a toast. One wears white and has dark flowing hair, the one in the middle turns her back to us in a deep red robe, and the third wears red over white. Their arms rise and their bodies seem to sway, as if caught mid-dance. At their feet the ground is scattered with fruit, grapes and a large gourd. The sky is a pale green. The scene feels like a harvest celebration, a moment of plenty shared among friends."},
"cups-04":{"up":"What you have is not bringing the satisfaction it once did, and you may be drifting through the days half-interested. The boredom is real, but it can also make you miss what is right in front of you. Sometimes this comes after a stretch of plenty, when even good things start to feel flat. Sometimes it is a mood that makes small annoyances seem bigger than they are. Taking time to reflect is healthy. Just do not stay inside the fog so long that a fresh invitation passes unnoticed. Look up. Somebody may be offering you something new, and it deserves at least a fair look before you wave it away.","rev":"The fog is starting to lift. After a period of withdrawal or restlessness, you may suddenly notice the opportunity you had been overlooking, or feel ready to rejoin the world. New people, new ideas and new ways of seeing things could arrive, and a quiet hunch may be pointing you somewhere worth going. Trust that instinct, but check it against reality. On the other side, you might still be so turned inward that you keep rejecting good things out of habit. Ask yourself honestly which it is. The answer is often as simple as saying yes to one invitation and seeing how it feels.","loveUp":"You may feel restless or uninspired in love. If you are single, dating might seem like more effort than it is worth, and you could overlook someone genuinely interesting. If you are in a relationship, routine may be dulling your appreciation. Try looking at the person or possibilities in front of you with fresh eyes.","loveRev":"Interest in love is returning. If you are single, you may feel ready to meet people again, and a new connection could catch your attention. If you are partnered, you might rediscover what drew you together. Accept the invitation to reconnect, whether it comes from someone else or from inside you.","workUp":"Work may feel stale, and you might be going through the motions. Before deciding nothing here interests you, look around. An offer, project or idea may be on the table that you have not really considered. Take a pause to reflect if you need it, then give new options a fair hearing.","workRev":"Motivation is coming back. You may finally notice an opportunity that was there all along, or feel curious about learning something new. Follow up on it. If you are still rejecting every suggestion out of habit, ask what you are protecting yourself from, and try saying yes to one small change.","picture":"A young man sits cross-legged beneath a tree on a grassy hill, arms folded across his chest. His eyes are cast down toward three golden cups standing in a row on the grass before him. From a small cloud on the left, a hand reaches out offering a fourth cup, and he does not seem to notice it. He wears a green tunic over red sleeves, with pale blue leggings. Behind him, a distant hill and a small bush sit under a pale green sky. His closed posture suggests someone turned so far inward that a new gift goes unseen."},
"cups-05":{"up":"Something has spilled, and you are standing over it. A plan that fell through, a friendship that cooled, a hope you carried for a long time and then had to set down: the sadness is real, and it deserves to be felt rather than rushed. Sometimes it is an outcome that did arrive, just not in the shape you were hoping for. Grief keeps its own pace. The catch is that it can narrow your gaze until the loss is the only thing you see. Some of what you had is still intact, maybe people, maybe skills, maybe a part of the plan that can be saved. You do not have to feel better yet. When you are ready, turn your head and take stock of what remains.","rev":"The heaviest part of the sorrow is starting to lift, and you are beginning to turn around. It may not feel like a big moment. It might be the first morning you do not reach for the old ache, or a call from someone who reminds you that you are not alone. Reconnection is part of this: old friends, family ties and people who share your roots or your values stepping back into view. There can also be a pull the other way, a habit of replaying the loss because moving on feels disloyal to it. Honor what happened, then pick up the cups that are still full. Recovery usually begins quietly, with one small choice to look forward.","loveUp":"A disappointment in love may still be stinging, whether it is a breakup, a date that fizzled or a rough patch with a partner. Let yourself feel it without deciding it defines you. If you are partnered, notice what is still good between you before dwelling on what went wrong. If you are single, remember the love in your life that has not gone anywhere.","loveRev":"Old heartache is loosening its grip. You may be ready to stop measuring every new person against the one who hurt you, or to stop reopening an argument with a partner that has already been settled. Friends and family can help here. Let people back in, and allow your future to be something other than a replay of the past.","workUp":"A setback at work, like a missed promotion, a project that was cut or feedback that landed hard, may be taking up most of your attention. Give yourself a moment to be disappointed. Then look at what survived: the skills you built, the colleagues who respect you, the parts of the work that still matter to you. That is your starting point.","workRev":"You are starting to move past a professional letdown, or you are being asked to. Reconnecting with former colleagues, mentors or allies could open a door you did not expect. If you keep replaying what went wrong, try writing it down once, pulling the lesson out of it, and then turning your attention to the next concrete step.","picture":"A figure in a long black cloak stands with head bowed, staring down at three golden cups tipped over on the ground, their red and green contents spilled out. Behind the figure, two cups still stand upright, unnoticed. The sky is a flat, muted tan. Beyond, a river runs through green land, crossed by a pale stone bridge on the right, with a small stone building and dark trees on the far bank at the left. The heavy black cloak speaks of mourning, while the bridge and the two standing cups hint that a way forward is still there."},
"cups-06":{"up":"Something from your past is sweetening the present. A childhood place, an old song, a friend who knew you before you had to be so grown up: memories like these can remind you who you were before life got complicated. There is real kindness in this moment, the simple, uncalculated kind, like sharing something only because you want the other person to have it. Let yourself enjoy that warmth. It can also point to fresh connections that feel oddly familiar, or a new setting where you get to be playful again. Take the comfort the past offers, and carry its generosity forward into how you treat the people around you now.","rev":"You may be holding on to an old version of yourself, a relationship or a place, and measuring everything now against how it used to be. Nostalgia is lovely as a visit and heavy as a home. When you keep reaching back, the present starts to feel thin by comparison, and new chances slip by unnoticed. Turned upside down, the card points you toward what is coming rather than what has gone. That does not mean throwing the memories away. It means letting them be a foundation instead of a hiding place. Ask what the old days actually gave you, maybe safety, play or belonging, and look for ways to build that into your life as it is today.","loveUp":"Tenderness and ease come to the front. If you are in a relationship, revisiting a place or ritual from your early days together could bring back the sweetness. If you are single, you may find yourself drawn to people who feel familiar and kind, maybe someone you have known for years. Innocent, playful affection is favored over high drama.","loveRev":"Comparing a current partner, or every new date, to someone from years ago can keep you from seeing who is actually in front of you. If an old flame keeps coming to mind, ask what you truly miss: the person, or who you were back then. Let the past stay a fond memory and give the present a fair chance.","workUp":"Your history is an asset right now. An old skill, a former colleague or a project you once loved may be worth revisiting. Warm, good-hearted working relationships are highlighted, and so is generosity, like helping a newer teammate or sharing credit freely. A new workplace might also feel surprisingly familiar and welcoming.","workRev":"Doing things the way they have always been done may be holding you back. If you keep talking about how good things were under an old manager or in a past role, it could be time to look ahead. What is coming asks for fresh ideas. Keep the lessons, drop the longing, and pay attention to where things are actually headed.","picture":"In a sunny village courtyard, a taller child in a red hood and blue-green tunic bends toward a smaller child, offering a golden cup filled with a white star-shaped flower. The little one wears a red headscarf and a white dotted dress and looks up at the gift. Four more cups with the same white blooms stand in a row in front of them, and another sits on a stone pedestal carved with a shield bearing an X. A square stone tower and a steep-roofed house fill the background under a pale sky. Everything here feels safe, gentle and a little old-fashioned."},
"cups-07":{"up":"Your mind is full of possibilities, and not all of them are as real as they look. Daydreams, fantasies and a dozen tempting options may be floating in front of you: the dream house, the fresh start in a new city, the version of a person you have built up in your head. Imagination is a gift, and some of these visions could lead somewhere good. But nothing here is solid yet, and choices made while you are dazzled tend to crumble later. Before you reach for one, test it against real life. Ask what it would actually take, what it would cost, and whether you want the thing itself or only the feeling of wanting it.","rev":"The fog is starting to lift. After a stretch of drifting between options, you may feel ready to pick one and put your energy behind it. That is real progress. Clarity rarely arrives as a thunderbolt; more often it shows up as a quiet sense that one path matters more to you than the rest. Trust that. There is a flip side worth watching: getting so fixed on a single fantasy that you refuse to see its flaws, or staying lost in daydreams because deciding feels risky. Either way, the task is the same. Name what you truly want, make a plan with real steps in it, and let the other shiny options go.","loveUp":"Romance may feel full of maybes. You could be weighing several people, or picturing an ideal partner who does not quite exist. If you are in a relationship, watch for fantasy standing in for honest conversation. Enjoy the daydreams, but get to know the actual person in front of you, and let them show you who they are.","loveRev":"You are getting clearer about what you want in love, and that makes choosing easier. You may stop entertaining connections that only live in your imagination and put your heart where it has a real chance. If you are partnered, a clearer shared vision can bring you closer. Say out loud what you are looking for.","workUp":"Plenty of ideas, offers or side projects are competing for your attention, and some look better from a distance than they will up close. Before committing, gather facts, ask direct questions and picture an ordinary Tuesday doing the work. The most glittering option is not always the one that holds up once the excitement fades.","workRev":"Focus is returning. You may finally be ready to choose one direction and give it real effort instead of spreading yourself thin. Write the goal down, break it into steps and set a realistic timeline. If you catch yourself chasing a single idea with no reality check, pause long enough to test it against the facts.","picture":"A dark figure, seen only in silhouette from behind, raises one arm toward seven golden cups floating on a bank of gray clouds. Each cup holds a different vision: a young curly-haired head, a veiled shape glowing with red light, a snake rising over the rim, a tower on a rock, a heap of spilling jewels, a laurel wreath and a winged dragon. The sky behind is a cool blue-green. Because the viewer stands in shadow, the cups seem to glow with promise, yet they rest on clouds, a reminder of how much of what we crave is imagined."},
"cups-08":{"up":"Sometimes the bravest thing is to leave something that is not broken, only finished. You may have put real effort into a situation, a role, a habit or a relationship, and now you can feel that it no longer fills you. What once seemed important may turn out to matter less than you thought. Walking away here is a choice, not a failure. It is the decision to look for something deeper, even when you cannot yet see where the road goes. You do not have to tear anything down on your way out. Thank it for what it gave you, gather yourself, and follow the pull toward what feels more true.","rev":"You may be lingering where you have already decided, deep down, that you do not belong. Fear of the unknown, guilt about letting people down, or plain habit can keep your feet planted long after your heart has moved on. Notice if you keep saying 'one more month' about the same thing. There is a brighter side too. Sometimes the restlessness passes and you realize that what you have is genuinely good, worth staying for and worth celebrating. The key is honesty. Are you staying because it still feeds you, or because leaving feels too hard? Only you can tell the difference, and the question deserves some quiet time.","loveUp":"Something in your love life may feel emotionally complete, even if nothing dramatic went wrong. If you are partnered, it may be time for a real conversation about whether you are both still growing, or whether you need more depth together. If you are single, you might step back from dating patterns that leave you empty and look for something richer.","loveRev":"Staying in a connection out of habit, or hesitating to move on from one that has already ended, can keep you stuck. On the other hand, you may discover that the relationship you nearly walked away from still holds real joy. Be honest with yourself about which is true, and respect the other person's right to make their own choices too.","workUp":"You may be outgrowing a role, a project or a whole line of work. It is okay to want more meaning than a paycheck and a title. Start by naming what feels missing, then explore quietly through conversations, courses or side projects. Leaving behind what no longer fits can be a thoughtful, gradual process rather than a dramatic exit.","workRev":"You may be hanging on in a role or project that stopped working for you a while ago, telling yourself the timing is not right. Or you may be surprised to find fresh satisfaction right where you are. Either way, look clearly at what you are getting from the work and what it is costing you, then make a deliberate choice.","picture":"Under a pale green sky, a figure in a red cloak and red boots walks away from us with a staff, heading toward dark, rocky mountains. In the foreground eight golden cups are neatly stacked, five below and three above, with a noticeable gap in the top row. A stretch of water lies between the cups and the hills. Overhead, a crescent moon curves around a golden disk with a calm, closed-eyed face. The careful stacking shows effort, while the gap and the traveler's turned back speak of something missing and a quiet decision to go looking for it."},
"cups-09":{"up":"A wish is within reach, or it may already have come true. There is a deep, simple contentment here: good food, good company, a comfortable home, a goal you set and actually met. Let yourself enjoy it. Plenty of people rush past their own successes, already worrying about the next thing, and miss the part where they get to feel satisfied. Success, advantage and a sense of ease in your body and surroundings are all favored. Take stock of how far you have come and savor it without apology. Being content does not make you lazy. It gives you a steady, grateful base from which to decide what you want next, and it tends to make you generous with others.","rev":"You may have gotten what you wanted and found it strangely hollow, or you may be reaching for more of something that stopped making you happy a while ago. Overindulgence, whether in food, spending, praise or comfort, can quietly dull the pleasure it promises. There can also be a smugness that keeps you from noticing small mistakes piling up. None of this is a verdict. It is a nudge to get honest about what truly fulfills you. Sometimes the answer is freedom, sometimes loyalty to a deeper value, sometimes simply admitting that the goal was not the right one. Real contentment tends to come from truth, not from having more.","loveUp":"Happiness in love feels within reach. If you are partnered, enjoy a stretch of ease and mutual appreciation, and say out loud what you are grateful for. If you are single, you may feel genuinely content on your own, which is an attractive and steady place to meet someone from. Let yourself want what you want.","loveRev":"Something that looks ideal from the outside may not feel as fulfilling as you expected. You might be chasing surface pleasures or getting comfortable in a way that skips real closeness. Whether single or partnered, ask what would make you feel truly met, and be honest if the answer differs from what you have been pursuing.","workUp":"Recognition, progress or a goal reached may bring a well-earned sense of satisfaction. Enjoy it and let others celebrate with you. It is also a good moment to notice what went right so you can repeat it. Confidence built on real results gives you a solid foundation for whatever you take on next.","workRev":"Success on paper may not be turning into satisfaction. You could be coasting on past wins while small errors add up, or chasing status that does not actually matter to you. Check the details, and ask whether your goals still reflect your values. Integrity and a sense of freedom may bring more fulfillment than another milestone.","picture":"A stout, round-faced man sits on a plain wooden bench, arms folded across his chest, wearing a satisfied smile. He has on a red cap with a red plume, a loose white robe marked with dark stripes, red stockings and soft yellow shoes. Behind him a curved stand draped in pale blue cloth holds nine golden cups in a neat arc, like trophies on display. The background is a warm, solid yellow. His folded arms and direct gaze suggest pride and comfort, and perhaps a hint of self-satisfaction about everything he has gathered."},
"cups-10":{"up":"Your heart has somewhere to rest. There is a sense of belonging here that goes beyond a single good moment: a home where you are welcome as you are, people who love you, friendships that feel like family. Maybe that is a household, a chosen family, a close community or the town you live in. It is the feeling of the whole picture fitting together. Let yourself notice it and be thankful for it. It can also point to someone who is looking out for your interests, quietly taking care of things on your behalf. Harmony like this grows from everyday kindness, so keep tending it with small, steady acts of care.","rev":"From the outside, everything may look fine. Underneath, though, something is off: a family keeping up appearances, a friendship held together by polite silence, a home where resentment simmers. The pressure to look happy can become its own burden. Tension that has been pushed down may rise into a real argument, which can be uncomfortable but also clarifying. You do not need to tear everything apart. Start by naming, gently and honestly, what is not working for you. Harmony that is real can handle a hard conversation. The goal is not a perfect picture. It is a home or circle where people feel safe enough to be truthful.","loveUp":"Love feels warm, secure and shared. If you are in a relationship, you may sense a strong partnership, a shared vision for home and the future, and real emotional safety. If you are single, the love of friends and family can fill your life, and you are free to build the kind of home that truly suits you.","loveRev":"Harmony in love may be more performance than reality right now. A partnership might look ideal to others while real needs go unspoken, or family pressure may be shaping your choices. If you are single, beware of chasing a perfect picture instead of a genuine connection. Honest conversations bring you closer to the real thing.","workUp":"Your workplace may feel like a genuine community, with teammates who back each other up and shared values that make the effort meaningful. Balance between work and home is also favored, and someone may be quietly looking out for your interests. Appreciate the people around you and help build the culture you want to be part of.","workRev":"A team that seems harmonious may be hiding friction, unspoken complaints or clashing values. The gap between how things look and how they feel could be wearing on you. Consider raising concerns constructively before they boil over, and check whether your work life is crowding out the relationships that matter most to you.","picture":"A bright rainbow arcs across a pale sky, with ten golden cups set along its curve. Beneath it a man in a red tunic and a woman in a blue-green gown stand close, each with an arm around the other and their free arms raised toward the rainbow. Beside them two small children dance in a circle, holding hands. Ahead stretches a green landscape with a winding river, rounded trees and a little house with a red roof. The couple face away from us, looking at what they share. Everything here speaks of home, joy and a family finding its place together."},
"cups-11":{"up":"A tender feeling or a gentle surprise is arriving. It might be a sweet message, an invitation, a creative idea that bubbles up from nowhere, or a first flutter of interest in someone. There is something young and open in this energy, willing to be moved and a little dreamy. It may describe a person in your life, often a kind, sensitive young person or someone new to their feelings, who wants to help or connect. It can also describe you, learning to trust your intuition and take your emotions seriously. Say yes to curiosity. Keep a notebook handy, listen to your hunches, and let yourself be delighted by small things.","rev":"Feelings are present, but they are not turning into anything solid. You may be swept up in a crush, a creative whim or a sentimental mood that fades before you act on it. Or someone around you may be long on sweet words and short on follow-through, charming in a way that does not quite ring true. There can also be a tendency to take small things too personally, or to hide in daydreams when a real conversation is needed. Whether this is you or another person, the invitation is the same: let feelings be real enough to lead to action. Check what is being promised, and notice whether it is actually delivered.","loveUp":"New or renewed feelings are stirring. If you are single, a flirtatious message, a sweet gesture or a surprising spark could brighten your days. If you are partnered, small romantic surprises and playful vulnerability can reawaken tenderness between you. Be open, a little brave, and willing to show what you feel.","loveRev":"Watch for emotional immaturity, your own or someone else's. Sweet words without consistent actions, mixed signals or a crush that lives mostly in your imagination can leave you confused. Whether single or partnered, focus on what people actually do. Take your own feelings seriously, and speak them plainly rather than hinting.","workUp":"A creative spark or a promising message could arrive at work. It is a good time for learning, experimenting and bringing imagination to your tasks. A younger colleague or newcomer may bring fresh ideas worth hearing. If you are the newcomer, your eagerness and sensitivity are strengths, so let them show.","workRev":"Good intentions at work may not be turning into results. A creative idea might stay a daydream, or someone may be promising more than they can deliver. Be wary of flattery that seems to have an agenda. Ground your inspiration in concrete steps, and hold yourself and others to follow-through.","picture":"A young man stands on a pale shore with the blue-green sea rolling behind him. He wears a blue-green tunic patterned with red flowers, puffed red sleeves, red tights, orange boots and a soft blue-green hat with a long scarf draped over his shoulder. One hand rests on his hip. In the other he holds a golden cup, and a small fish pokes its head out of it, looking back at him. He studies it with calm interest. The surprise of the fish suggests unexpected feelings and ideas rising from somewhere deep."},
"cups-12":{"up":"An invitation, an offer or a heartfelt approach is heading your way. It may be a romantic proposal, a friend reaching out with good news, or an opportunity that speaks to your ideals and your imagination. This energy moves at a gentle, graceful pace, leading with feeling rather than force. As a person, it can describe someone charming and sincere who brings warmth and possibility into your life. As a role, it invites you to be that person: to follow your heart, make the thoughtful gesture, and act on what you care about. Welcome what arrives, and let your own sincerity show in how you respond.","rev":"Charm is plentiful, but substance may be missing. An offer that sounds wonderful could turn out to have strings or gaps, or someone may say all the right things without meaning them. You might notice mood swings, broken plans or a pattern of promises that never quite land. It can also point to your own tendency to romanticize, to chase the ideal and avoid the practical parts. None of this means you should close your heart. It means slowing down, asking questions and seeing whether actions match words. Genuine feeling survives a little scrutiny. If something falls apart when you look closely, it was never as solid as it seemed.","loveUp":"Romance is in the air. If you are single, someone may approach with sincere interest, or you may feel moved to make a heartfelt gesture yourself. If you are in a relationship, expect more thoughtfulness and emotional openness. Enjoy the courtship, and let both of you set the pace together.","loveRev":"Be cautious of grand romantic words that are not backed by steady behavior. Someone may be more in love with the idea of love than with you, or you may be doing the same. Whether dating or partnered, notice patterns rather than promises, and choose people whose actions line up with what they say.","workUp":"An appealing offer or invitation may come through, perhaps involving creative or people-centered work. Approach it with enthusiasm and a genuine heart. Diplomacy and a warm, persuasive manner help you now, so bring them to negotiations and presentations. Just make sure the practical details match the vision.","workRev":"A proposal that sounds too good to be true deserves careful questions. Watch for colleagues or contacts who promise much and deliver little, and read the fine print on anything you agree to. If you are the one overpromising, scale back to what you can actually do and keep your word.","picture":"A knight in silver armor rides a white horse at a slow, calm walk, holding a golden cup out in front of him as if offering it. Small wings sprout from his helmet and his heels. His tunic is patterned with blue waves and red fish. The horse lowers its head as it steps toward a winding stream. Behind them rises a red, craggy hill, with distant trees and fields beyond. Nothing here is rushed. The wings hint at imagination, and the careful pace suggests a messenger carrying something precious and in no hurry to spill it."},
"cups-13":{"up":"Deep feeling, held with steadiness, is your strength right now. Compassion, intuition and emotional wisdom are all available to you, and so is the ability to be there for others without losing yourself. It may point to a person in your life, someone caring, perceptive and devoted, who listens well and supports you without trying to fix you. It can also describe the role you are being asked to play: trusting your inner knowing, holding space for someone else, or treating your own feelings with the same kindness you give others. Quiet reflection sharpens your sense of what is true. Let your heart lead, and let your calm keep it steady.","rev":"Emotions may be spilling over their banks. You could be absorbing everyone else's moods, giving until you are drained, or feeling so much that it becomes hard to think clearly. Sometimes the reversal shows the opposite: feelings shut away because they seem too big to handle. In another person, it can describe someone whose warmth is inconsistent, caring one day and unreliable or manipulative the next. If it is you, be gentle but honest with yourself. Boundaries are a form of care, not a lack of it. Take some quiet time alone, notice what is yours to carry and what is not, and let the water settle before making decisions.","loveUp":"Love is nurturing and emotionally rich. If you are partnered, deep empathy and attentiveness strengthen your bond. If you are single, you may meet someone who values emotional depth, or you may simply enjoy caring for yourself and the people you love. Trust your intuition about who feels safe.","loveRev":"Emotional overwhelm or codependent patterns may be affecting your love life. You might be giving too much, expecting a partner to read your mind, or losing yourself in someone else's needs. If you are single, check whether you are drawn to people you feel you must rescue. Gentle boundaries protect the love you want.","workUp":"Emotional intelligence is your advantage at work. Listening closely, reading the room and supporting colleagues builds trust and influence. Creative or caring work flourishes now. A compassionate mentor or colleague may be a valuable ally, or you may be playing that role for someone else.","workRev":"Workplace stress may be seeping into your emotional life, or other people's problems may keep landing on your desk. Guard your energy. Try not to take criticism too personally, and be wary of colleagues who use sympathy to get their way. Clear boundaries and a little distance will help you think straight.","picture":"A queen in a white gown and a shimmering blue-gray cape sits on a throne at the very edge of the sea. The throne is carved with small cherub figures, and a tiny sea child sits near its base. She holds an ornate lidded cup, shaped almost like a little church with carved handles, and gazes at it intently. Water laps at her feet across a shore of colorful pebbles, and a golden headland rises in the distance under a pale green sky. Unlike the open cups elsewhere in the suit, hers is closed, suggesting feelings and insights kept safely held within."},
"cups-14":{"up":"Emotional maturity is the gift here: feeling deeply while staying calm, kind and fair. You can listen with your heart and still make a sound decision, a rare balance that others notice and trust. It may point to a person in your life, perhaps a mentor, advisor, counselor or creative professional, who is responsible, generous with support and steady under pressure. It can also describe the role you are stepping into, whether leading a team, guiding a family through a hard patch, or simply staying centered while others react. Let compassion and good judgment work together. Being steady does not mean being cold. It means your feelings serve you rather than steer you.","rev":"Moods may be running the show instead of wisdom. That can look like sudden coldness, withdrawal, or someone using emotion, or a show of kindness, to control a situation. In another person, it might describe a figure of authority who seems supportive but has their own agenda, or whose warmth comes and goes depending on what they want. In yourself, it may show up as bottling everything up until it leaks out sideways, or as letting a bad mood make your decisions. None of this is permanent. Step back, breathe, and name what you actually feel. Fairness returns when honesty and composure come back together.","loveUp":"Love is steady, mature and kind. If you are partnered, emotional stability and generous support make the relationship feel safe. If you are single, you may be drawn to people who are emotionally grounded, or be that grounded presence yourself. Patience and calm communication help any connection grow.","loveRev":"Emotional unavailability, mood swings or subtle manipulation may be clouding your love life. A partner or date may seem caring but hold back real warmth, or you may be doing this yourself to stay in control. Pay attention to consistency, and ask for the openness you need rather than guessing.","workUp":"Calm leadership and diplomacy serve you well at work. You can handle difficult conversations with tact and keep people feeling valued while still making firm decisions. A wise, supportive mentor may help you, or you may be the steady hand others rely on. Fairness and creativity go hand in hand here.","workRev":"Watch for someone in authority whose help comes with hidden strings, or for office politics dressed up as kindness. You might also notice your own moods affecting how you lead or respond to others. Keep records, stay fair and professional, and take a pause before reacting to anything that stirs you up.","picture":"A king sits on a broad stone throne that seems to float on a restless sea, waves washing around its base. He wears a red and gold crown, a pale blue robe and a heavy olive-green cloak lined with red, with a small fish-shaped pendant at his chest. In his right hand he holds a golden cup, and in his left a short golden scepter. A fish leaps from the waves on one side, and a ship with a red sail passes on the other. His calm face suggests steady command over emotional waters."},
"swords-01":{"up":"A thought arrives with a sharp edge, and suddenly you can see what was fuzzy before. Maybe it is the sentence that finally explains why a situation has felt wrong, or the decision you have circled for weeks landing in one clean moment. The energy here is strong and forceful, the kind that cuts through excuses and breaks a stalemate. Use it. Say the true thing, write the plan down, draw the line that needs drawing. Clarity like this is powerful in every direction, so aim it with care: it can open a door or slam one. When your mind is this sharp, the win comes from being honest and precise, not from being loud.","rev":"Your mind is sharp right now, but the edge may be pointed at the wrong target. Perhaps you are using being right as a way to score points, cutting someone down with a perfect argument instead of solving the actual problem. Or the clarity has turned inward and harsh, and you are slicing your own ideas apart before they have a chance to breathe. Too much force can wreck the very thing it meant to fix. Notice where your words are landing and what they cost. Truth still matters, and so does timing. Soften the delivery, ask one question before making your point, and let understanding be the goal rather than victory.","loveUp":"Honest words clear the air. If you are in a relationship, a frank conversation could cut through a misunderstanding that has lingered too long. If you are single, you may suddenly see exactly what you want, and what you will no longer accept. Say it simply and kindly, and let the other person respond in their own way.","loveRev":"Be careful not to turn honesty into a weapon. In a relationship, winning an argument can quietly cost you closeness. If you are single, a sharp inner critic may be dismissing other people, or yourself, too fast. Pause before the cutting remark, and ask whether you want to be right or want to be understood.","workUp":"A breakthrough idea or a clear decision can move work forward fast. This is a good moment to name the real problem in a meeting, write the proposal, or set a firm boundary around your time. Keep your reasoning clean and your language direct, and people are likely to follow your thinking.","workRev":"Sharp thinking can turn into sharp elbows. You might be tempted to win a debate at a colleague's expense, or to pick apart a plan so thoroughly that nothing is left to build on. Channel the edge into solving the problem. Credit others, check your tone, and let the facts do the persuading.","picture":"A white hand reaches out of a gray, curling cloud on the left, gripping a single upright sword by its hilt. The tip of the blade passes through a golden crown set with red stones. From one side of the crown hangs a sprig of leaves dotted with red berries, and from the other a long green frond. Small golden drops fall through the air around the blade. Along the bottom, a low range of brown and blue-green mountains stretches across the card. The raised sword and crown suggest a clear idea rising to victory, with open space all around it for the mind to work."},
"swords-02":{"up":"You are holding two options at arm's length and refusing to let either one in. It can look like calm, even like strength, and in a way it is: you have found a balance that keeps things steady. But the balance comes from not looking. Maybe you are avoiding a decision between two jobs, two people, or two versions of a story, because choosing means losing something. There is a truce quality here too, a peace kept carefully between parties who are still on guard. Give yourself credit for the composure. Then ask what you would see if you lowered your arms and took off the blindfold. Stalemates rarely resolve on their own.","rev":"The blindfold is slipping, and what you have been avoiding comes into view. That can feel uncomfortable at first. You may notice that someone has not been straight with you, or that you have not been straight with yourself about what you want. A decision you kept on hold is now pressing, and the careful truce is harder to maintain. This is not a punishment. It is the moment when real information finally reaches you. Look at it honestly, even if it stings, and resist the urge to cover your eyes again. Once you see the whole picture, choosing becomes simpler, and the tension you have been carrying can finally let go.","loveUp":"Something is being held in careful balance. In a relationship, you may be keeping the peace by not raising a real question. If you are single, you might be weighing two possibilities, or keeping your heart guarded while you decide. Tenderness is possible here, but it needs you to let your arms down a little.","loveRev":"Hidden things tend to surface now. You might see more clearly whether someone has been honest with you, or admit where you have been holding back the truth yourself. Whether you are dating or committed, clear sight is a gift, even when it is uncomfortable. Let what you learn guide your next step rather than retreating into not knowing.","workUp":"A decision at work is stuck, perhaps between two projects, two offers, or two sides of a disagreement. Holding steady buys you time, but not forever. Gather the facts you have been avoiding, spell out what each path truly costs, and set yourself a gentle deadline. Neutral ground works best when it leads somewhere.","workRev":"Information that was hidden is coming out, maybe about a colleague's agenda, a project's real status, or your own reluctance to commit. Be alert to anyone telling different people different stories, and make sure you are not doing it yourself. Once you see clearly, make the call you have been postponing and communicate it plainly.","picture":"A woman in a long white gown sits on a stone bench with a white blindfold over her eyes and her arms crossed over her chest. In each hand she holds a long sword, and the two blades rise past her shoulders in a wide V. Behind her stretches blue-green water dotted with dark rocks, and a low orange shoreline runs along the horizon. A thin yellow crescent moon hangs in the upper right of a pale green sky. The crossed arms and covered eyes suggest a choice held off by refusing to look, while the moon hints at quiet intuition underneath."},
"swords-03":{"up":"Something hurts, and there is no point pretending otherwise. It might be a harsh word, a letdown, a separation, or a truth that landed exactly where you are most tender. The gift here is honesty: the pain is out in the open, named and visible, rather than buried where it can fester. Let yourself feel it. Cry if you need to, talk to someone who listens well, write down what happened in plain words. Grief and disappointment move through faster when they are acknowledged. A rift or an absence can be real without being the end of your story. For now, simply tell the truth about what stings.","rev":"The worst of the hurt is starting to ease, even if it still aches when you press on it. Healing is underway, like a scab forming over a cut. The risk now is picking at it: replaying the conversation, rereading old messages, or getting lost in confused thoughts about what went wrong and whose fault it was. That loop can keep you distracted and foggy. Another version of this energy is holding pain inside instead of letting it out, which only slows things down. Be gentle with yourself. Let your mind rest from the story, and give your heart the time it needs to knit itself back together.","loveUp":"Heartache may be part of the picture right now, whether from a disagreement, a distance between you and a partner, or a hope that did not work out. If you are single, an old hurt may still be sore. Name it honestly, to yourself and to anyone who deserves to hear it. Acknowledging pain is the first step toward moving through it.","loveRev":"A romantic hurt is slowly mending. In a relationship, you may both be ready to talk more calmly about what happened. If you are single, you might notice you think about a past heartbreak less often. Resist reopening it just to check whether it still hurts. Let healing take its time, and let the other person take theirs.","workUp":"A disappointment at work might sting, perhaps criticism that felt personal, a project that fell through, or a split within the team. Give yourself a moment to feel it before reacting. Then look for the useful truth inside the hard news, and talk it through with someone you trust rather than letting it simmer.","workRev":"The sting of a setback at work is fading, though it may still color how you think. Watch for distraction and second-guessing, the kind that has you replaying a mistake instead of learning from it. Take the lesson, let go of the rest, and bring your attention back to the task in front of you.","picture":"A large red heart hangs in the center of the card, pierced by three swords. One blade runs straight down through the middle, and two more cross it at angles from either side, their points emerging beneath the heart. Behind it, pale gray clouds fill the upper part of the card, and long slanting streaks of rain fall across a tan background. There are no people and no landscape, only the heart, the blades and the weather. The bare design suggests grief stated plainly, without decoration, and the rain hints at tears that help wash the pain through."},
"swords-04":{"up":"You need to stop, and not as a sign of failure. After a stretch of stress, conflict or constant thinking, the wise move is to put the swords down for a while and recover. That might mean a real day off, a quiet weekend, a walk without your phone, or simply saying no to one more commitment. Rest is not wasted time: it is how the mind sorts what has happened and gathers strength for what comes next. Some solitude may help too, a chance to hear your own thoughts without everyone else's. Stay alert in a calm way, but let the fight wait. You will think more clearly once you have caught your breath.","rev":"Rest is being offered and you keep turning it down. Maybe you feel guilty slowing down, or you worry that if you stop, everything will fall apart. So you push on, tired and wired, and your thinking gets foggier the harder you push. There is a better way to manage this. Turned around, the card also points to careful planning: pacing your energy, budgeting your time, and making small, sensible adjustments instead of dramatic ones. You do not need a long retreat to benefit. Take the break you have been postponing, plan your week with some margin in it, and let steady, measured effort bring you the success you are after.","loveUp":"A pause can be healthy for love. In a relationship, it may help to step back from a recurring argument and return to it rested. If you are single, time on your own could be exactly what restores you before you open your heart again. Quiet is not the same as distance. Sometimes it is a form of care.","loveRev":"You may be running on empty and bringing that tiredness into your relationships. Partners can feel it when you are present in body but somewhere else in mind. If you are dating, you might be filling every evening to avoid being alone with your thoughts. Slow down on purpose, and plan time to recharge before you reconnect.","workUp":"Step back from the grind for a bit. A short break, a lighter week, or a day to think without meetings could restore the focus you have been missing. Use the quiet to review what matters most and let the rest wait. Good ideas often arrive when you stop chasing them.","workRev":"Burnout is a risk if you keep refusing to pause. At the same time, this is a good moment for careful organization: trimming commitments, pacing deadlines, and using your time and energy sensibly. Measured planning now can lead to steady progress. Protect some recovery time on your calendar and treat it as seriously as any meeting.","picture":"A carved figure of a knight in armor lies on top of a stone tomb, his hands pressed together in prayer over his chest. Three swords hang point down on the wall above him, and a fourth lies flat along the side of the tomb below. In the upper left corner, a stained glass window shows two figures in bright red, green, blue and gold. The rest of the room is washed in muted tan and pale yellow, and nothing moves. Everything here suggests stillness, prayer and deliberate rest, a pause taken in a quiet, sheltered place."},
"swords-05":{"up":"Someone is walking away with the prize, but not with much honor. Maybe you won an argument and lost the room, or someone else got their way by playing dirty and left everyone else deflated. The card asks you to look at the whole cost of a conflict, not just the scoreboard. Sometimes the wise move is to put a fight down, because winning it would mean becoming someone you do not want to be. If you are on the losing side, walking away can be the stronger choice. If you are the one gathering up the swords, notice who is no longer standing next to you. A victory that leaves you alone is an expensive one.","rev":"The fight is over, and now the bill comes due. You may be feeling the loss more heavily than expected, whether you were the one who won or the one who walked away. Regret, embarrassment or lingering resentment can hang in the air long after the shouting stops. There may be sorrow here too, for a friendship or a sense of trust that took a hit. The good news is that this is the moment when repair becomes possible. You can apologize, reach out, or simply decide not to reopen an old battle. Being right turns out to be worth less than you thought. Choose peace where you can, and forgive yourself where you need to.","loveUp":"A conflict in love may be turning into a contest, with each person trying to win rather than understand. If you are in a relationship, ask whether proving your point is worth the distance it creates. If you are single, notice any old pattern of fighting to be right. Connection grows when both people can set their defenses down.","loveRev":"After an argument or a breakup, you may be counting what it cost. Regret and hurt pride can linger on both sides. If there is room to mend things, a sincere apology can soften a lot. If it is truly over, let it be over with dignity, and let the other person make their own choices.","workUp":"Office politics may be running hot. Someone could be grabbing credit, cutting corners, or pushing for a win that leaves the team resentful, and it might even be you. Ask what the victory really costs. Sometimes the smart move is to let a small battle go and protect your reputation and working relationships instead.","workRev":"The aftermath of a clash at work is sinking in. Maybe a win did not feel as good as expected, or a loss left you embarrassed. Use this as a turning point: acknowledge your part, rebuild trust where you can, and decide which battles are really worth fighting next time.","picture":"A young man with red hair stands in the foreground, looking back over his shoulder with a smirk. He carries two swords propped against his shoulder and rests his other hand on a third, its point on the ground. Two more swords lie scattered at his feet. Behind him, two other figures walk away toward the water with their backs turned, one small and hunched. His tunic is green over red sleeves and red leggings, and jagged gray clouds streak across a pale sky. The scene suggests a hollow win, one person collecting the spoils while the others leave defeated."},
"swords-06":{"up":"You are leaving rough water behind, even if the boat still feels heavy. This is a transition away from something difficult toward a place that is steadier, whether that means a literal move, a trip, a change of routine, or simply a quieter state of mind. The journey may be a little sad, and you may carry some of your worries along, but the direction is good. Accept help if it is offered, and let someone else steer for a while if you need it. Practical solutions matter more than perfect ones right now. Keep going. The far shore is calmer than where you started, and each push of the pole brings you closer.","rev":"You are trying to move on, but you have packed the old trouble into the boat with you. Maybe you left a situation physically and are still living in it in your head, or you keep postponing a transition because the unfinished business feels too heavy. Another thread here is speaking up: something may need to be said out loud, a confession or an honest declaration, before you can truly leave it behind. Getting the truth into the open can lighten the load more than any distance. Ask yourself what you are still carrying that you could set down. The crossing gets easier once the boat holds less.","loveUp":"Love is moving into calmer water. In a relationship, you may be leaving a rough patch behind and finding a gentler rhythm together. If you are single, you could be putting distance between yourself and an old heartache, which makes room for something new. Travel or a change of scene may also play a pleasant part.","loveRev":"Old baggage may be riding along into your love life. If you are partnered, a past argument or unspoken feeling might need airing before things can settle. If you are single, feelings you have not expressed, to someone else or to yourself, may be asking for words. Honest speech lightens the load, whatever the other person chooses to do with it.","workUp":"A transition at work is underway, perhaps a new team, a new approach, or a move away from a stressful situation. Progress may be gradual rather than dramatic. Accept support and practical fixes, and keep your eyes on where you are heading. Calmer conditions lie ahead if you stay steady.","workRev":"You may be switching roles or projects but bringing old stress along with you. Unresolved tensions or a problem you never addressed can follow you into the next chapter. Consider whether something needs to be said openly, a concern raised or a mistake owned, so you can start fresh with less weight on your shoulders.","picture":"A ferryman in a red tunic stands at the back of a small boat, pushing it across the water with a long black pole. In the middle of the boat sits a figure wrapped in an orange and yellow cloak, head bowed, beside a small child. Six swords stand upright in the front of the boat. The water near the boat on the right is rippled, while the stretch ahead lies smooth, and a far shore with trees rises in the distance. The quiet passengers and the steady pole suggest a sad but necessary crossing toward somewhere calmer."},
"swords-07":{"up":"A clever plan is in motion, and not everything is being done out in the open. Sometimes this is healthy strategy: working quietly, choosing your moment, taking only what you can carry and leaving the rest. Sometimes it is sneakier, a shortcut, a half-truth, or someone slipping away with what is not theirs. Ask which version you are living. If you are the one planning, be honest with yourself about whether your methods would hold up in daylight. If you suspect someone else, keep your eyes open without leaping to accusations. Confidence and ingenuity are real strengths. Just make sure the plan does not depend on nobody ever noticing.","rev":"Secrets are getting harder to keep, and that may come as a relief. You might feel ready to come clean about something, or to stop running a strategy that required you to hide your real intentions. Good advice is also coming your way. Someone may offer counsel worth hearing, and the lesson is to actually take it rather than nodding along and doing what you had planned anyway. Be wary of gossip too, both what you hear and what you pass on. Being open can feel exposing, but it saves an enormous amount of energy. Clear the air, listen to wise voices, and let your next move be one you can explain.","loveUp":"Something may be going unspoken in your love life. In a relationship, one of you could be keeping thoughts or plans private. If you are single, you may be playing it cool, strategizing instead of showing your hand. A little discretion is fine, but trust grows from honesty. Ask yourself what you would say if you were not managing the outcome.","loveRev":"Honesty is ready to come forward. In a relationship, a confession or a frank talk could clear the air. If you are single, you might let go of games and say what you really feel. Listen to the good advice of friends who know you well, and be careful not to feed gossip.","workUp":"Work calls for strategy and discretion. You may need to move quietly on a plan, protect an idea until it is ready, or find a smart way around an obstacle. Keep your methods clean, though. Watch for anyone cutting corners or taking credit, and keep a record of your own contributions.","workRev":"It may be time to be upfront about something at work: a mistake, a change of plan, or a concern you have been holding back. A mentor or colleague may offer advice you would be wise to follow instead of politely ignoring. Stay out of office gossip, and let transparency rebuild any trust that slipped.","picture":"A man in a red cap and a pale yellow tunic tiptoes away from a camp, carrying five swords bundled in his arms by their blades. He glances back over his shoulder with a sly half smile. Two more swords stay standing upright in the ground behind him. On the right, striped and patterned tents fly small dark flags, and his red boots are trimmed with dark fur. Everything sits against a bright, flat yellow sky. His careful steps and backward glance suggest cleverness and stealth, a plan carried out while others are not watching."},
"swords-08":{"up":"You feel trapped, and the feeling is real enough to hurt. Yet look closely: much of what holds you in place is the story you are telling about the situation. Maybe criticism or bad news has knocked your confidence, and now every option looks blocked. You tell yourself you cannot leave, cannot ask, cannot change anything. Some of the limits are genuine, but others are thoughts dressed up as walls. Start small. Question one belief about what is impossible. Ask for the help or information you have been assuming you would not get. Often there is more room to move than it seems, and the first step is simply noticing where the gaps are.","rev":"The ropes are starting to loosen. You may be seeing, bit by bit, that you have more options than you thought, or that the pressure you felt was partly of your own making. Freedom does not always arrive all at once, and there may still be friction: people who resist your changes, worries that flare up, surprises that throw you off balance. That is normal when you begin moving again after feeling stuck. Keep going anyway. Take one practical step, then another. Pay attention to what is actually happening rather than the worst-case story. As the blindfold loosens, you get the chance to walk out on your own terms.","loveUp":"You may feel stuck in love, whether in a relationship pattern that keeps repeating or in the belief that you will never meet the right person. Some of that feeling comes from old stories you tell yourself. Question them gently. There are usually more choices than it seems, including the choice to speak up about what you need.","loveRev":"A sense of freedom is returning. In a relationship, you may find new ways to talk about something that once felt impossible. If you are single, you might be letting go of the idea that you are stuck or unlovable. Expect some bumps along the way, and keep choosing what feels honest and healthy for you.","workUp":"Work may feel like a narrow space right now, with rules, criticism, or limited options closing in. Before deciding there is no way out, list what is truly fixed and what is only assumed. Ask questions, gather information, and look for small openings. Your situation may be more flexible than your fears suggest.","workRev":"You are finding your way out of a tight spot at work. New options or insights are appearing, even if there is still some opposition or unexpected friction to handle. Keep moving steadily, check the facts before reacting, and trust your growing sense that you can shape your own path here.","picture":"A woman in a long red dress stands blindfolded, her upper body wrapped in pale bands of cloth. Eight swords are planted point down in the ground around her like a loose fence, three on her left and five on her right. She stands on wet, reddish ground scattered with puddles, and behind her, on a rocky rise, a castle with red roofs sits in the distance. The sky above is pale and empty. Her feet are unbound and there are gaps between the blades, which suggests the trap is less complete than it feels."},
"swords-09":{"up":"Worry has taken over the night shift. You may be lying awake with thoughts that multiply, replaying a disappointment or bracing for the worst. In the dark, everything feels bigger and more certain than it really is. The distress is real, and it deserves care, but the story your anxious mind tells is not a forecast. Try to separate what has actually happened from what you fear might happen. Write the worries down so they live outside your head for a while. Talk to someone you trust in the morning. Despair tends to shrink when it is shared and looked at plainly, and daylight can do a surprising amount to put things back in proportion.","rev":"The night is ending, and the worries that felt enormous look smaller in daylight. You may be starting to see which fears were exaggerated and which have a real basis you can address. That distinction matters: a reasonable concern can be acted on, while a runaway thought only needs to be recognized for what it is. There may still be some shame or doubt clinging to you, or a sense of being locked in your own head. Be patient with yourself. Reach out, open the curtains, get the facts. What seemed impossible to face at 3am often turns out to be something you can handle one practical step at a time.","loveUp":"Anxiety may be crowding into your love life. You might lie awake wondering where you stand with someone, or replaying a painful exchange. If you are single, worry about the future can feel heavy. Share these fears with someone safe, and check your thoughts against what you actually know rather than what you imagine.","loveRev":"The fog of worry is lifting. You may begin to see which relationship fears were real and which were fueled by late-night imagination. If a doubt is grounded in facts, you can address it openly. If you are single, let go of any shame about the past. Clearer, calmer conversations are within reach.","workUp":"Work stress may be following you home and keeping you up at night. Deadlines, mistakes, or disappointments can look catastrophic after midnight. Write your concerns down, sort them into what you can influence and what you cannot, and talk them through with a trusted colleague or friend. Morning clarity often reveals a workable path.","workRev":"The panic around a work issue is easing. You can now separate reasonable concerns, which deserve action, from fears that were blown out of proportion. If you had good reason to be cautious about someone, trust that instinct and verify quietly. Otherwise, let the worry go and focus on practical next steps.","picture":"A figure sits upright in bed in a pale nightgown, face buried in both hands. Nine swords hang horizontally across a pitch-black background, stacked one above another like bars. Over the bed lies a quilt of green and yellow squares, some holding red roses and others small drawn symbols. The side of the bed is decorated with a carved panel. The darkness and the stacked blades suggest the weight of worry pressing in at night, while the bright, homely quilt hints that comfort is closer than it feels in that moment."},
"swords-10":{"up":"Something has reached its end, completely and unmistakably. A situation you have been struggling with, whether a relationship, a job, or a way of thinking, has run its course, and there is no more pretending it might recover. That can bring real sadness and exhaustion. You may feel flattened, as if you have taken every possible blow. Let yourself grieve. Yet there is a strange relief in a final ending: the worst has already happened, and you no longer need to brace for it. Look toward the horizon, where the light is changing. Once there is nothing left to hold onto, you are free to begin again, slowly and on your own terms.","rev":"The worst is behind you, even if you are not fully back on your feet. Recovery is happening slowly, one small improvement at a time, and that is how it should be. You may notice energy returning, or some small wins arriving after a long hard stretch. Enjoy them, while remembering that good turns come and go, so keep building on solid ground rather than counting on one lucky break. Another side of this energy is resisting an ending that is already complete, clinging to what has finished because letting go feels like admitting defeat. Let it be over. Getting up is a process, and you are already in it.","loveUp":"A chapter in love may be closing, whether it is a relationship, a hope, or an old pattern you are finally done repeating. It can hurt deeply. Give yourself room to grieve, and lean on friends. If you are single, this may be the moment you stop replaying the past. Endings clear the ground for something healthier.","loveRev":"Healing after heartbreak is underway. You may feel steadier than you did, even if you are still tender. In a relationship, you might be recovering from a painful rough patch together. If you are single, let the past stay in the past rather than reopening it. Small, hopeful steps now build real strength.","workUp":"A work situation may have reached its limit: a project ending, a role that no longer fits, or a conflict that has exhausted everyone. Accept that this chapter is done instead of fighting for more of the same. Rest, reflect on what you learned, and let the clean slate show you what you want to build next.","workRev":"After a tough stretch at work, things are slowly improving. You may see some gains, recognition, or a bit more influence, but treat them as a foundation rather than a finish line. Keep your footing steady, learn from what went wrong, and let go of any lingering grudges about how things ended.","picture":"A figure lies face down along the bottom of the card, a red cloth draped over his body, with ten swords standing upright along his back. Above him the sky is black, but near the horizon a band of golden yellow light breaks beneath the dark clouds. Below that glow lie calm blue-green water and a line of distant hills. His outstretched hand rests on the ground. The black sky makes the scene feel final and complete, while the glow along the horizon suggests that this ending is also the edge of a new day."},
"swords-11":{"up":"Your mind is wide awake, scanning the room and asking the questions other people skip. Something has caught your attention, a detail that does not add up or a plan that looks a little too neat, and you want to understand it properly. Keep watching, and gather facts before you pick a side. The figure here might be a sharp, curious person around you, often someone younger or new to the situation, or it might be you, taking on the role of the observer. Either way, there is a note about privacy: someone may be more interested in your business than they should be, or you may be tempted to pry into theirs. Stay alert, and stay fair about what you look into.","rev":"Alertness has tipped over into suspicion. You may be checking and rechecking, reading hidden meanings into short texts, or assuming bad intentions before anyone has done anything. Watchfulness is healthy until it starts feeding on itself. The opposite can happen too: you have been so busy guarding one corner that something else catches you unprepared, and a piece of news lands as a genuine surprise. If a person in your life fits this picture right now, they may be gossiping, snooping, or talking faster than they think. Ask yourself what you actually know and what you are only guessing. Prepare for the things you can prepare for, and let the imagined plots go.","loveUp":"You are paying close attention to how someone really treats you, not just to what they say, and that is wise. If you are single, ask the curious questions on a first date and notice the answers. If you are in a relationship, bring up the thing you have been wondering about in a calm, direct way. Honest questions build trust when they are asked in the open.","loveRev":"Doubt may be running the show. Scrolling through someone's feed for clues or reading too much into a slow reply rarely brings peace. If you are partnered, say what is worrying you instead of investigating quietly. If you are single, notice whether old hurts are making you wary of people who have done nothing wrong. Trust grows from conversation, not surveillance.","workUp":"Your eye for detail is an asset at work right now. Research the proposal, read the fine print, and ask the question nobody else in the meeting will. You may be new to a role and learning fast, which is fine. Keep your own plans close until they are ready, and think twice about what you share in group chats.","workRev":"Office gossip or a climate of mistrust could be pulling focus away from the actual work. You might be second-guessing a colleague without evidence, or someone may be watching your moves more closely than feels comfortable. Check the facts before reacting. Also look for anything you have left unprepared, since a surprise is much easier to handle when your basics are in order.","picture":"A young figure stands on a rough rise of green and yellow ground, gripping a tall sword upright with both hands. The tunic is rose pink with yellow sleeves and a black belt, and bright red boots plant the feet wide apart. Hair whips back in the wind as the head turns to look over one shoulder. Billowing clouds crowd in behind, a flock of birds scatters across a pale green sky, and a small tree bends at the far left. The raised ground and the backward glance suggest someone on lookout, alert to whatever might come from any direction."},
"swords-12":{"up":"Things are moving fast, and someone is charging straight at the issue with no patience for small talk. That someone might be you, finally ready to say the direct thing and act on it, or it might be a bold, sharp-tongued person who has just ridden into your life. There is real courage here and real skill: the ability to cut through confusion, defend what matters, and push past resistance. It can also stir up conflict, because speed and bluntness do not leave much room for other people's feelings. Use the momentum to break a stalemate or to finally tackle what you have been avoiding. Just glance at who is standing in your path before you ride through.","rev":"Speed without direction is making a mess. You or someone near you may be rushing decisions, starting arguments that did not need to happen, or promising far more than can be delivered. When the charge loses its aim, energy pours into drama, grand gestures, or fighting for the sake of it. There may also be a clash with someone who will not listen to reason, and pushing harder is unlikely to win that one. The invitation is to rein the horse in. Pick one goal, check your facts, and choose words that can land without wounding. Being direct still works. Being reckless mostly creates cleanup.","loveUp":"Someone may be moving quickly and saying exactly what they want, or you may be the one ready to speak plainly. If you are single, a fast, exciting connection could sweep in, and it is fine to enjoy the pace while you get to know each other. If you are partnered, a frank talk clears the air. Keep the directness kind.","loveRev":"Heated words or impulsive moves could be causing damage. Maybe an argument escalated because nobody paused, or you rushed into something before really knowing the other person. Whether you are single or in a relationship, take a breath before the next message or big declaration. Another person's pace deserves as much respect as yours, and quick is not the same as sincere.","workUp":"Momentum is on your side. This is a good time to push a stalled project forward, argue clearly for your idea, or take on a hard problem head on. Your competence and confidence can carry the room. Stay open to the objections that come up, because answering them well is part of what makes your case strong.","workRev":"Haste may be causing errors, or a colleague is bulldozing through decisions without consulting anyone. Clashes over small points can eat up whole days. Before you fire off the reply or launch the plan, check that you have the details right. If someone at work refuses to listen, pick your battles carefully and put important points in writing.","picture":"An armored knight charges full tilt on a pale horse, sword raised high overhead as the pair race toward the left edge of the card. A red cloak and a red plume stream back from the helmet, and the horse's harness is painted with small yellow butterflies. The mane flies and the legs stretch out in a gallop. Clouds are torn into ragged strips across the sky, and a couple of thin trees at the left bend hard in the wind. Everything in the picture is in motion, which captures both the thrill of decisive action and the risk of outrunning your own judgment."},
"swords-13":{"up":"Clear sight is the gift on offer, even if it has been earned through some hard experience. The figure here knows sorrow, absence or separation firsthand, and has come out the other side unwilling to pretend. She might be a person in your life, often a woman, who tells you the truth kindly but without sugar. Or she might be you, standing on your own after a loss or a disappointment and seeing things exactly as they are. Honest boundaries, sharp perception and independence are strengths now. You do not need a comforting story to get through this. You need the facts, a steady mind, and permission to feel what you feel while still thinking clearly.","rev":"Clarity has hardened into coldness. You may be cutting people off before they can disappoint you, or using sharp words to keep hurt at a distance. Old grief that was never fully felt can do this, turning honesty into criticism and caution into suspicion. Reversed, the Queen can also point to someone around you who is judgmental, two-faced or quietly working against your interests, so pay attention to actions and not just charm. In either case, the answer is not to stop being perceptive. It is to let a little warmth back in. Ask whether you are protecting yourself or punishing others, and notice which honest words you could say more gently.","loveUp":"Honesty matters more to you than romance right now, and that is healthy. If you are single, you may be enjoying your independence and refusing to settle for less than real respect. If you are in a relationship, speak plainly about what you need. Past hurts have taught you something useful, and you can carry that wisdom without carrying the pain.","loveRev":"Walls may be up. A sharp comment, a cool silence or an old heartbreak could be keeping love at arm's length. If you are partnered, notice whether criticism has replaced conversation. If you are single, ask whether you are judging people too quickly to give anyone a fair chance. Being careful is wise, but closing every door can leave you lonelier than you want to be.","workUp":"Your clear head is exactly what the situation needs. You can see through vague promises and inflated reports, and people may come to you for a straight answer. Say what you see, set firm boundaries around your time, and make decisions based on evidence. A frank mentor, or your own frankness, helps everyone move faster.","workRev":"Criticism at work may be crossing into harshness, whether it is coming from you or aimed at you. A colleague may be friendly to your face and dismissive behind your back, or you may be so guarded that teammates stop sharing. Keep your standards, but deliver feedback with care. Write down important agreements, and watch actions more closely than words.","picture":"A crowned queen sits in profile on a tall grey stone throne, facing right. She holds a long sword straight up in one hand and lifts the other hand open, as if inviting someone forward or giving a clear signal. Her cloak is patterned like scattered clouds over a grey gown, and a winged child's face is carved into the throne. Below her a bank of clouds rolls in, dark trees stand at the lower left, and a single bird flies high in a pale blue sky. The upright sword and the open hand suggest firm judgment held together with a willingness to listen."},
"swords-14":{"up":"A decision needs to be made on principle, not on mood. Here is the energy of clear judgment: weighing the evidence, hearing each side, and ruling fairly even when it is uncomfortable. You might meet it as a person in your life with real authority, an expert or advisor whose thinking is sharp and whose word carries weight. Or it could be you, stepping into the role of the one who decides and sets the standard. Intellect and fairness lead, backed by the confidence to stand by a conclusion. Use your head. Say what the rules are, apply them evenly, and let your integrity be the thing people can count on.","rev":"Logic has lost its warmth, and power may be used carelessly. Reversed, the King can describe someone around you who wins arguments by being cold, uses rules as weapons, or bends the truth to keep control. It can also be a mirror: are you so sure you are right that you have stopped listening? Sharp minds turn cruel when they forget there are people on the other side of every judgment. If a long-running dispute or grudge is draining you, now is a good moment to ask whether it is worth continuing. Clear thinking and compassion can work together. Bring both back into the room before deciding anything big.","loveUp":"Clear communication and mutual respect are the foundation now. If you are partnered, a frank conversation about expectations can make things stronger. If you are single, you may be drawn to someone thoughtful and principled, or you may be setting your own standards more firmly. Knowing what you will and will not accept is a form of self-respect.","loveRev":"Coldness or control may be creeping in. One person might be treating disagreements like debates to win, or holding back affection to keep the upper hand. Whether you are single or in a relationship, notice where your head is overruling your heart for protection. Love needs fairness, but it also needs tenderness, and nobody should feel judged in their own home.","workUp":"Your judgment is trusted, so use it. This is a good time to make a firm call, set clear policies, or give honest counsel. You may be working with a sharp, senior figure whose standards are high, and meeting them earns respect. Decide based on evidence and principle, then explain your reasoning so others can follow it.","workRev":"Authority is being used badly, or someone is hiding behind rules to avoid responsibility. A manager may be rigid and unfeeling, or you may be leading with logic alone and losing people's goodwill. Watch for decisions that look fair on paper but ignore the people they affect. If a workplace conflict has dragged on too long, consider what it would take to close it.","picture":"A king sits facing straight out from his throne, meeting your eyes with a calm, stern expression. He holds a long sword upright, tilted slightly to one side. A pale blue-green robe falls to his feet beneath a deep purple cloak lined with red, and a red hood frames his face under a golden crown. The dark throne back is carved with a butterfly near the top. Two birds fly off to the right, clouds gather on both sides, and dark trees stand low in the distance. His steady gaze and firm grip suggest authority that rests on reason and composure."},
"pentacles-01":{"up":"Something solid is being offered to you. It may be a job lead, a place to live, a chance to learn a trade, or simply the resources and energy to start building something real. Unlike a passing idea, this opening has weight: you can hold it in your hands and do something with it. Deep contentment and a sense of security come from tending it well, day after day. Pay attention to practical chances that arrive quickly or through good information. The seed is here, and it is a good one. What grows from it depends on whether you plant it, water it and give it time. Take the first grounded step.","rev":"An opening is there, but it is not being picked up. Maybe you are waiting for a sign clearer than this one, or the opportunity looks too ordinary to take seriously. Either way, the chance can slip past quietly. There is another side too: when comfort and money arrive, they can bring new worries, like greed, fear of losing it, or choices made only for material reasons. Information may also be less reliable than it looks, so check the details before you commit. Good things still surround you. The question is whether they are serving you or running you. Look at one practical offer you have been ignoring, and ask whether your hesitation is wisdom or just fear of starting.","loveUp":"A relationship with real foundations is possible. If you are single, a new connection could start from something grounded, like shared routines, shared values or a friend's introduction. If you are partnered, small practical acts of care, a meal cooked or a plan followed through, build lasting security. Love that shows up consistently is its own kind of treasure.","loveRev":"A promising connection might be left to fade because no one takes the first practical step. Or material concerns, like money worries or lifestyle comparisons, are crowding out affection. Whether you are single or partnered, ask what would make a relationship feel secure to you, then act on it. Comfort is lovely, but it is not the same thing as closeness.","workUp":"A concrete opportunity may appear: a new role, a client, a project with real resources behind it, or training that opens doors. Treat it seriously and give it steady effort. The early groundwork you do now will matter more than any big gesture later. Good news or useful information can arrive quickly, so stay ready to respond.","workRev":"An offer or opening might be sitting unused because you doubt it or feel too busy to follow through. Or a focus on money alone could be steering decisions that should also weigh people and long-term fit. Check the details carefully, since information may not be as reliable as it seems. Small, steady action beats waiting for the perfect chance.","picture":"A pale hand reaches out of a grey cloud on the left, palm up, offering a large golden coin marked with a five-pointed star. Faint rays of light spread around the hand. Below lies a tidy garden of dark green hedges dotted with red flowers, and an arch cut through the hedge opens onto a yellow path leading toward distant blue mountains. The background is a warm cream. The gift seems to come from beyond, but the path is on the ground, which suggests that a real opportunity is being handed over and you are the one who has to walk it."},
"pentacles-02":{"up":"Life is asking you to juggle, and you are doing better at it than you might think. Two demands, two jobs, two budgets, two priorities: somehow you are keeping them all in motion. A light touch helps. When you can treat the balancing act a little like a game, stress loosens its grip, and many of the troubles on your mind turn out to be bigger in your imagination than in real life. Watch for messages and paperwork that need a response, and expect some shifting ground. Flexibility is your strength here. Keep your rhythm, stay adaptable, and allow yourself some fun while you carry the load.","rev":"Too many balls are in the air, and the smile may be a bit forced. You could be pretending you are fine while quietly dropping things, or saying yes to plans you have no energy for. When the dance loses its ease, the answer is not to try harder. Instead of letting something fall by accident, choose what to set down on purpose: a commitment, a side project, or a social obligation you only keep out of guilt. Look at your calendar and your messages with honest eyes. Letters, forms and written agreements need extra care right now, so read them closely. A simpler rhythm lets you enjoy what you keep.","loveUp":"Balancing love with everything else takes some creativity now. If you are partnered, find playful ways to connect even on busy weeks: a short walk, a silly text, a shared joke. If you are single, you might be enjoying a few light connections or dividing your time between dating and other priorities. Keep it fun and keep it honest.","loveRev":"One of you may be stretched too thin to show up fully. If you are in a relationship, talk about what can come off the schedule so there is room for each other. If you are single, notice whether you are going through the motions of dating without really enjoying it. It is fine to pause and choose what matters most.","workUp":"Multitasking is the job right now, and you can handle it. Prioritize, keep a running list, and adapt as deadlines shift. Written communication matters, so respond to emails and messages promptly. A flexible, good-humored approach will carry you through a busy period better than rigid planning. Some worries are simply louder than the actual risks.","workRev":"Your workload has outgrown your capacity. Rather than hiding it, decide which task to drop or hand off, and tell the people affected. Double-check written details, agreements or figures before signing off, since mistakes creep in when you are rushed. Putting on a cheerful face while overwhelmed only delays the reset you need.","picture":"A young man in a tall red hat dances on one foot, holding a golden coin marked with a star in each hand. A green band loops around both coins in a figure-eight, joining them in one continuous flow. He wears an orange tunic with a jagged hem, red leggings and soft green shoes. Behind him, high rolling waves lift two ships, one riding a steep crest. The sky is a pale green. His easy step against the rough sea suggests keeping your balance and good humor while circumstances rise and fall around you."},
"pentacles-03":{"up":"Good work is getting noticed. Skill, care and cooperation are coming together, and the result can be something people respect. You may be learning a craft, collaborating on a project, or bringing your expertise to a group that needs it. Each person brings something different, whether vision, planning or hands-on ability, and the mix is what makes the work excellent. Listen to feedback and offer yours clearly. Recognition, even a bit of reputation, can follow from doing things properly rather than quickly. Take pride in the details. When you commit to quality and treat others as real partners, what you build lasts.","rev":"Effort is not lining up. Maybe you are giving far more to a shared project than others are, or maybe you have been coasting and the work shows it. Standards can slip into mediocrity here, and small egos or petty disputes get in the way of doing something well. Communication may be poor, with plans nobody agreed on or roles that were never made clear. None of this is final. Sit down with the people involved and match expectations to effort. If the team cannot align, focus on the part you control and do it with care. Quality returns when respect and clarity do.","loveUp":"Love works best as a partnership of equals right now. If you are in a relationship, building something together, a home, a routine, a shared goal, strengthens your bond. If you are single, you might meet someone through work, a class or a group project, where you get to see how they cooperate. Respect for each other's strengths is attractive.","loveRev":"One person may be putting in more effort than the other, or the two of you are working toward different pictures of the future. If you are partnered, talk about what each of you contributes and what feels unbalanced. If you are single, notice whether you are settling for half-hearted effort from people you date. You deserve someone who shows up.","workUp":"Teamwork and craftsmanship are in the spotlight. Your skills are valued, and collaborating with people whose strengths differ from yours can produce excellent results. Ask for input from those with more experience, share your own expertise generously, and pay attention to quality. Careful, visible work now builds your professional reputation.","workRev":"The team may be out of sync. Unequal workloads, unclear roles or petty rivalries could be dragging the standard of work down. Rather than quietly resenting it, raise the issue and clarify who does what. Check whether your own effort matches your goals. Doing the job properly, even when others do not, protects your good name.","picture":"Inside a stone church, a craftsman stands on a red bench beneath a pointed arch, holding a tool as he turns toward two visitors. One, dressed in dark clothing, holds a large sheet of plans. Beside him stands a figure wrapped in a bright red hooded cloak. Above them, three pentacles are carved into a trefoil pattern in the arch, with a carved flower below. The worker's raised position and the visitors' attention suggest skill that is being recognized, and a project that needs both the people with the vision and the hands that build."},
"pentacles-04":{"up":"You are holding tight to what you have, and there is good reason for it. Stability matters, and whether you worked hard for your security or received it through family, you want to protect it. That instinct can be healthy: being careful with money, setting boundaries, and not spending energy carelessly. The question is how firm the grip has become. Clinging too hard can leave no room for new experiences or generosity, and a life run entirely on control can start to feel small. Appreciate the foundation you have. Then ask whether you are guarding it with care or with fear, and whether your hands are free for anything new.","rev":"The grip is loosening, for better and for worse. You may be ready to share more, open up, or let go of possessions and habits that no longer serve you, and that generosity can feel wonderful. At the same time, change like this can come with delays, obstacles or pushback from people who liked things the way they were. Plans may stall while everyone adjusts, so be patient with the in-between stage. If you have been clutching control out of fear, practice releasing a little at a time. If instead you are letting go too fast, set sensible limits. Balance between security and openness is the goal.","loveUp":"Security is a big theme in love right now. If you are partnered, you may be focused on building stability together, though possessiveness can creep in if either of you feels uncertain. If you are single, you might be guarding your heart carefully. Protecting yourself is fair. Just make sure you are not closing off every chance of closeness.","loveRev":"Old defenses may be softening and letting more warmth in. If you are in a relationship, you might feel ready to share more openly, or you may need to loosen control and trust your partner. If you are single, letting down your guard could feel risky but freeing. Change may take time, so be patient with the pace.","workUp":"You are focused on security and on keeping what you have built. That can mean protecting your position, being careful with resources, or holding firm on a boundary. Stability is valuable, but watch for rigidity that blocks growth. Consider where a bit of openness, like sharing credit or trying a new approach, could serve you better than holding on.","workRev":"A controlling habit or a tight, scarcity mindset may be relaxing, bringing a chance for more collaboration and generosity. You might also run into delays, red tape or resistance as things shift. Be patient with the process and keep observing what is working. Letting go of control where it makes sense can open doors that were shut.","picture":"A crowned figure is planted in front of a city skyline, hugging a golden pentacle tightly to his chest with both arms. Another pentacle rests on top of his crown, and one lies flat under each red shoe. He is wrapped in a dark cloak over a red robe, and his expression is watchful. Behind him rise towers and red-roofed buildings under a pale cream sky. Every coin is pinned in place by his body, which suggests security and ownership, but also a grip so tight that nothing can move in or out."},
"pentacles-05":{"up":"Times feel lean and a bit lonely. You may be dealing with a money worry, a loss of support, or simply the sense of standing outside a warmth others seem to enjoy. Hardship like this is real, and it is not a verdict on your worth. Notice, though, how easy it is to keep walking past the help that exists: a friend who offered, a community resource, a person who would listen if asked. Pride or exhaustion can keep your head down. Look up. You are not walking alone, either, since someone may be sharing the struggle with you. Clear reasoning and practical planning can gradually turn things around.","rev":"The worst of the cold may be easing. Help that was hard to see is coming into view, and you might be ready to accept it, knock on a door, or let someone in. Recovery can still be messy, though. Old disorder, scattered finances or strained relationships may take a while to settle, and the habits that led here need attention so the pattern does not repeat. Be gentle with yourself as you rebuild. If love has been under strain, an honest talk about what each person needs can help. Step toward the light in the window, one small action at a time, and let support count.","loveUp":"Love may feel strained by outside pressures, like money stress or isolation. If you are in a relationship, facing hard times together can deepen your bond when you lean on each other rather than withdrawing. If you are single, loneliness might feel sharp. Reach out to friends and communities that make you feel welcome, and remember that your value does not depend on circumstances.","loveRev":"A difficult stretch in love may be starting to turn around, though some tension could linger. If you are partnered, an honest look at what went wrong can help you rebuild. If you are single, you may be ready to open up again after feeling left out in the cold. Accept warmth when it is offered, and give it where you can.","workUp":"Work or finances may feel precarious right now, whether through reduced hours, a missed opportunity, or feeling overlooked. Focus on what you can control: practical planning, asking what support is available, and connecting with people who can offer guidance. Pride can stop you from asking, but help often sits closer than you think. Steady reasoning will carry you through.","workRev":"Recovery from a setback at work is possible, and you may finally notice resources or allies you had overlooked. Still, some disorder remains, and old habits, like scattering your energy or avoiding the hard numbers, need attention. Accept help, rebuild step by step, and be honest about what still needs fixing. Things improve when you stop going it alone.","picture":"Two ragged figures trudge through falling snow past a lit church window. One leans on wooden crutches, head bandaged and feet wrapped. The other, bent under a pink shawl over a green skirt, walks barefoot with her face turned down. Above them, a stained-glass window glows with five golden pentacles set among green vines and panes of red and blue, framed by a dark stone wall speckled with snow. Neither looks up at the warm light, which suggests hardship made heavier by feeling shut out, and help that may be nearer than it seems."},
"pentacles-06":{"up":"Giving and receiving are in motion. You may be in a position to help someone, share what you have, or offer your time and knowledge, or you may be the one who benefits from another person's generosity. Either way, the healthiest exchanges feel fair to both sides. Gifts, support and a sense of present comfort are highlighted, and gratitude comes easily. There is also a note of attention: this good moment is worth appreciating, but it may not last forever, so do not lean on it as if it were permanent. Share wisely, receive gracefully, and keep the balance honest so everyone involved keeps their dignity.","rev":"Generosity may have come with strings attached. Someone could be giving in order to control, or you might be helping out of obligation while quietly keeping score. Envy, jealousy and wishful thinking can distort the exchange, leaving you feeling either owed or indebted. There may also be a check on your ambitions, a reminder that not everything you want is within reach right now. Look honestly at the give and take in your life. Where does it feel uneven? Setting clear terms, or gently refusing help that costs too much, restores fairness. Real support leaves both people feeling respected, not smaller.","loveUp":"Love feels balanced and caring. If you are in a relationship, you may be giving and receiving support in equal measure, and small kindnesses count for a lot. If you are single, you might find satisfaction in friendships, volunteering or community, where affection is shared freely. Generosity of spirit makes you attractive and keeps connections healthy.","loveRev":"An imbalance in giving and receiving may be causing tension. One person might feel like they do all the caring, or affection may come with expectations attached. Whether you are partnered or single, notice any jealousy or scorekeeping. Healthy love gives freely and receives gratefully, without leaving anyone feeling beholden.","workUp":"Fair exchange is the theme at work. You might receive support, recognition or a well-earned reward, or be in a position to mentor and help others. Share credit and resources generously. Enjoy the present stability, but stay attentive rather than assuming it will always last. Good relationships with colleagues grow from fairness.","workRev":"Strings may be attached to support or opportunities at work. A mentor or boss might expect more in return than seems fair, or envy among colleagues could sour the atmosphere. Your ambitions may meet a temporary check. Clarify terms before accepting favors, and make sure your own generosity is not quietly draining you.","picture":"A well-dressed merchant in a red cloak and striped tunic stands between two kneeling people. He drops coins into the cupped hands of one and holds a balanced pair of scales in his other hand. The figure on the left wears a patched yellow cloak and looks up at him, and the one on the right, wrapped in blue-green, reaches out as well. Six golden pentacles float in the pale sky around them, and a small town tower rises in the distance. The scales suggest fairness, yet the kneeling figures remind you that giving always carries a balance of power."},
"pentacles-07":{"up":"You have put in real work, and now you are standing back to see what it has grown into. The harvest is not ready yet, but it is visible, and that pause matters. It gives you room to ask honest questions: is this effort paying off, is it the right crop, and what would you change next season? Think of a business you started, a skill you have been building, or a relationship you have tended. Progress in these things is slow and hard to see from one day to the next. Look closely at what has actually grown, count the wins as well as the gaps, and decide with a clear head whether to keep going, adjust, or plant something new.","rev":"Waiting is wearing on you. You planted something and it is not growing as fast as you hoped, so you keep digging it up to check the roots. That impatience can push you toward giving up too early, or toward pouring in more time and money out of worry rather than judgment. Sometimes the unease is about resources you have lent, time you have given, or promises someone made you, and you are not sure they will come good. Notice whether the worry is telling you something useful or just making noise. Slow growth is still growth. Set a fair point to review the results, then stop checking every day and let things develop.","loveUp":"Love that has been tended over time is ready for an honest look. If you are in a relationship, notice what you have built together and what still needs care. If you are single, reflect on what past connections have taught you before you rush into the next one. Good things are growing, and patience lets them ripen.","loveRev":"You may be frustrated that a connection is not moving faster, or quietly wondering whether it is worth the effort you keep putting in. That doubt deserves a calm conversation rather than a string of tests. If you are single, resist judging your whole love life by one slow season. Some things take longer to bloom, and you get to decide what you keep watering.","workUp":"A project or career path is far enough along that you can judge it fairly. Look at what your effort has actually produced, not what you feared or hoped it would. Measure results, ask for feedback, and decide where your energy goes next. Steady work is paying off, even if the full reward is still a little way off.","workRev":"Frustration with slow progress at work may be tempting you to abandon a plan before it has had time to prove itself. There may also be worry about money or effort you have committed on someone else's word. Instead of fretting, set clear checkpoints, ask direct questions, and give the work a fair season before judging it.","picture":"A young man in a red tunic, pale blue sleeves and orange boots leans on a long hoe, his hands folded on the handle and his chin resting on them. Beside him a leafy green vine climbs upward, and six gold pentacles hang among its leaves like ripening fruit. A seventh pentacle lies on the ground near his feet. The sky is plain and pale, the soil behind him dark and turned. He is not working in this moment, only looking. His tired, thoughtful pose suggests someone weighing the harvest and wondering what the next season will ask of him."},
"pentacles-08":{"up":"Skill is built one repetition at a time, and you are in the middle of that process. Whether you are learning a trade, mastering a new tool at work, or simply getting better at something you care about, progress comes from showing up and doing it again with attention. It is not glamorous, and nobody may be watching, yet each careful piece makes the next one easier. There is real satisfaction here too: the quiet pride of a job done well. You are often in the preparatory stage, so do not rush to the finish. Focus on the work in front of you, keep your standards high, and let your hands learn what your head already knows.","rev":"The work is getting done, but your heart may have left the room. Repeating the same tasks without care can turn craft into chore, and the results start to show it. Another version is perfectionism, polishing one piece forever while the rest waits. There can also be a pull to cut corners or to use cleverness to look impressive rather than to do good work, whether that pull comes from you or from someone around you. Ask what you are really practicing for. If the answer has faded, reconnect with what drew you to this skill, or admit it may be time to learn something new. A small change in approach can bring the care back.","loveUp":"Relationships grow through small, repeated acts of attention. If you are partnered, the everyday effort of a kind message, a shared chore or proper listening is building something solid. If you are single, you might be working on yourself: your habits, your boundaries, your sense of what you want. That practice is not a detour from love. It is part of preparing for it.","loveRev":"Routine may have slipped into autopilot. You might be showing up for a partner out of habit rather than presence, or putting all your energy into work and leaving little for the people you love. If you are single, notice whether you are going through the motions of dating without really engaging. A bit of fresh attention goes a long way.","workUp":"Your skills are growing, and the effort you put in now will count later. Training, an apprenticeship, a new role or a demanding project all fit here. Focus on quality, ask for feedback, and take pride in doing things properly. Steady, careful work builds a reputation that no shortcut can match.","workRev":"You may be putting in hours without much satisfaction, or chasing polish on details that no longer matter. Watch too for anyone, yourself included, using skill to look good rather than to deliver. Reconnect with the purpose of the work, set realistic standards, and consider whether you need a new challenge to stay engaged.","picture":"A young craftsman sits on a red wooden bench, a hammer in one hand and a chisel in the other, working a star into a gold pentacle. He wears a blue-green tunic with a dark apron, red stockings and red shoes. Six finished pentacles hang in a column down a tall wooden post beside him, and another lies on the ground by his bench. Far off to the left, a small town with red roofs and a tower sits under a pale sky. He has his back to the town, absorbed in the task, and the row of finished pieces shows patience paying off."},
"pentacles-09":{"up":"Comfort you earned yourself has a particular sweetness, and that is what surrounds you now. Through good judgment, patience and steady effort, you have built a life, or a corner of one, that feels safe and pleasant. You do not need anyone's permission to enjoy it. Independence is a strong theme: the ability to support yourself, make your own choices, and appreciate the finer things without apology. Maybe it is a home you have made your own, a skill that pays its way, or simply the calm of knowing you can handle things. Take a moment to notice how far you have come. Discernment got you here, and it will keep guiding you well.","rev":"The garden looks lovely, but the walls around it may be getting too high. Self-reliance is a strength until it becomes a reason to never ask for help or let anyone close. You might also be leaning on appearances, keeping up a picture of success while something underneath feels hollow or unsteady. Sometimes the card points to a plan that does not deliver what it promised, or to someone whose dealings are not quite honest, so read the fine print. None of it cancels what you have built. It asks you to check whether your comfort is still serving you, and to let people and fresh purpose back into the space you made.","loveUp":"You are whole on your own, and that makes you a better partner rather than a lonelier one. If you are single, enjoy your own company, keep your standards, and let anyone new meet you where you already stand. If you are in a relationship, bring your independence into it as a gift, two full lives sharing space instead of one leaning on the other.","loveRev":"Independence may be sliding into distance. You might be protecting your peace so carefully that there is no room for anyone else, or staying in something comfortable that no longer feels honest. If you are single, check whether high walls are keeping good people out. In a relationship, ask whether you are sharing your life or simply living alongside each other.","workUp":"Your efforts are paying off, and you have earned a measure of security and freedom. Take time to appreciate your results and enjoy the independence they bring. Keep using the careful judgment that got you here. Running your own show, leading a well-managed project or holding a role with real autonomy all fit this energy nicely.","workRev":"Something that looked solid at work may not be as secure as it seems. Double-check agreements, watch for promises that sound too polished, and avoid resting on past success. You might also be working so independently that you have cut yourself off from support. Ask for input and reconnect with colleagues before small issues grow.","picture":"A woman in a long white robe patterned with red flower shapes stands in a vineyard heavy with purple grapes. A small hooded bird perches on her raised, gloved hand, and her other hand rests on a stack of gold pentacles. Six pentacles are piled on one side of her and three more sit on the other. Behind her, trees and a distant house stand under a warm yellow sky, and a tiny snail crawls along the path at her feet. Everything around her looks cultivated and calm, the picture of a life she has tended with care."},
"pentacles-10":{"up":"What you are building is meant to last beyond a single season. Here the focus widens to family, home and the roots that hold generations together. It can speak of financial stability, a house full of history, or traditions handed down and kept alive. It can also be about the legacy you are creating now: values, habits and resources that will support the people who come after you. Success of this kind is not flashy. It is the sort that makes a place feel secure and lets everyone breathe a little easier. Honor where you come from, take care of what you have, and think about what you want to pass on.","rev":"Family matters or shared resources may be more tangled than you would like. Inheritance, whether it is money, a house, expectations or old patterns, can bring questions about fairness and who owes what. There may be a temptation to gamble with security, or a feeling that fortune is out of your hands. Sometimes a gift or unexpected support arrives from a surprising place, and sometimes a long-standing arrangement starts to wobble. Either way, the moment asks for honesty. Talk openly with the people involved, look carefully at what you are really carrying forward, and remember that you get to choose which traditions to keep and which to let go.","loveUp":"Love here looks like commitment and a shared future. If you are partnered, you may be thinking about building a home, blending families, or making plans that span years. If you are single, you might be drawn to someone who values stability and family as much as you do. Either way, the focus is on lasting bonds rather than passing sparks.","loveRev":"Family pressure, old expectations or money questions may be straining a relationship. You might feel caught between a partner and relatives, or unsure whether you want the traditional path at all. If you are single, notice whether inherited ideas about love are shaping your choices more than your own wishes. Honest talk can untangle a lot.","workUp":"Long-term thinking serves you well at work now. Building something durable, strengthening a family business, or creating systems that will outlast your own time in the role all fit this energy. Stability and reputation grow from consistent choices. Think about the legacy of your work and what you want it to stand for.","workRev":"Questions about shared resources, succession or long-held arrangements may be unsettling your work life. A risky shortcut might look tempting, or a stable setup may feel less certain than before. Slow down, get clear on the facts, and have direct conversations with the people involved before making any big move.","picture":"An old man with long white hair sits in the foreground in a richly patterned robe, and two white dogs press close beside him. Beyond, beneath a stone archway, a man with his back to us stands with a woman in red who turns toward him, and a small child peeks out at her side. Through the arch rise a tall pale tower and a house with an orange roof under a blue sky. Ten gold pentacles are spread across the whole scene. Three generations share one doorway, a picture of family, home and what passes between them."},
"pentacles-11":{"up":"A fresh start in the practical world is taking shape, and you are approaching it like a good student. You might be beginning a course, learning a new trade, or making the first genuine attempt at a goal you have talked about for ages. The energy is curious, patient and serious in the best way. It is less about instant results and more about laying groundwork. News or an opportunity connected to study, money or work may also reach you. As a person, this can be a young or new learner in your life who is eager and dependable. As a role, it is you being willing to start at the beginning and take the first step for real.","rev":"Plans have a way of staying plans, and that may be where you are. The idea is good and the notebook is full, but the first real step keeps getting pushed back. Sometimes the obstacle is distraction, or spending energy and money on comforts instead of the goal. Sometimes it is fear of being bad at something new. News that does not go your way can also knock your focus. As a person, this may be someone full of promise who struggles to follow through. As a role, it could be you. Pick one small, concrete action and do it soon. Learning only starts once you begin.","loveUp":"Love is in a learning phase. If you are single, you might meet someone through study or work, or simply be exploring what a healthy relationship looks like for you. If you are partnered, you may be discovering new sides of each other. Take it slow, be sincere, and let trust build step by step.","loveRev":"You may be dreaming about love more than taking part in it, or waiting for the perfect moment to speak. Someone might seem promising but hesitate to show up consistently, and that person may be you. Whether you are single or partnered, a small honest gesture teaches you more than endless imagining.","workUp":"A new skill, course or entry-level role could be the start of something solid. Approach it with curiosity and discipline. Ask questions, take notes, and build good habits from day one. Opportunities linked to learning or careful planning are favored, and small practical steps now set up bigger results later.","workRev":"A work goal may be stuck in the planning stage. Procrastination, scattered focus or unclear priorities might be holding you back, or disappointing news has taken the wind out of your sails. Break the goal into manageable pieces, choose the first task, and follow through before adding anything new.","picture":"A young man stands in a green meadow dotted with small red flowers, holding a single gold pentacle up in both hands and gazing at it intently. He wears a green tunic tied with a red sash, red stockings, brown boots and a red hood whose long tail falls over his shoulder. Behind him a clump of trees grows on one side, a ploughed field lies on the other, and a lone mountain rises in the distance under a bright yellow sky. His absorbed stare suggests a student fascinated by something he is only beginning to understand."},
"pentacles-12":{"up":"Slow and steady is not a weakness here. It is the whole method. Progress comes from showing up, keeping promises, and doing the unexciting tasks that others skip. You might be in a stretch of routine work, careful saving, or consistent training where results build quietly. The pace may feel plodding, but it is reliable, and reliability earns trust. As a person, this can be someone in your life who is dependable, patient and practical, the one who actually follows through. As a role, it asks you to be that person: responsible, thorough and willing to finish what you started. Keep your head down and keep moving forward.","rev":"Steadiness has turned into standing still. Routines that once kept you on track may now be keeping you stuck, and it is easy to confuse being busy with making progress. There can be discouragement underneath, a sense that effort is not going anywhere, which leads to coasting or carelessness. As a person, this may be someone capable who has lost momentum, or whose caution has hardened into stubbornness. As a role, notice if it is you. Change one small thing: a new approach, a fresh goal, a conversation you have avoided. You do not need to abandon your careful nature, just point it somewhere that feels alive again.","loveUp":"Love grows through consistency and small, dependable acts. If you are partnered, reliability and shared routines are strengthening your bond. If you are single, you may be drawn to someone steady and sincere, or you might be taking your time before committing. Slow is fine. Trust built carefully tends to last.","loveRev":"Things may feel stuck or predictable. A relationship could be running on routine without much warmth, or one person may be resisting any change at all. If you are single, you might be too cautious to take a chance. Try something new, alone or together, and gently shake up the pattern.","workUp":"Diligence and responsibility are paying off. You are the person people can count on, and that reputation matters. Stick with your plan, pay attention to details, and keep delivering. Progress may be gradual, but it is solid, and careful work now brings useful results over time.","workRev":"Work may feel stagnant, or you might be stuck in routines that no longer move you forward. There could be a sense of being underused, with plenty of ability and nowhere good to put it. Look for small ways to bring fresh energy, set a new target, or ask for a challenge that fits your skills.","picture":"An armored knight sits on a heavy black horse that stands completely still on a small rise. He holds a single gold pentacle in his gloved hand and studies it closely. Sprigs of green leaves crown his helmet and the horse's head, and red straps and a red saddle cloth stand out against the dark animal. Behind him lie ploughed fields in neat red furrows under a yellow sky. Nothing in the scene is in a hurry. The planted stance and the patient gaze suggest care, method and a job that will be seen through."},
"pentacles-13":{"up":"Care that is practical, warm and grounded sits at the center of things. Think of someone who makes a home feel welcoming, keeps the budget in order, and still has time to ask how you are really doing. That generous, capable energy is available to you now, whether you are giving it or receiving it. Security comes from tending what you have with attention: your routines, your space, your work and the people you love. As a person, this may be a nurturing, resourceful figure in your life. As a role, it invites you to be that for yourself as well as for others. Enjoy the comforts you have created and share them freely.","rev":"Giving has tipped into giving too much. You might be looking after everyone else while your own needs sit at the bottom of the list, and the imbalance is starting to show as tiredness, resentment or worry. Fear and mistrust can creep in too, with a nagging sense that security could slip away, or suspicion about other people's motives. As a person, this may be someone whose care comes with control or anxiety. As a role, notice whether that is you. Put yourself back on the list. Ask for help, say no to one extra task, and let yourself receive a little of the care you give so well.","loveUp":"Love here is nurturing and generous. If you are in a relationship, you may be creating a warm, secure home together and caring for each other in practical ways. If you are single, focus on building a life that feels abundant and welcoming, the kind of steadiness that people who share your values will recognize.","loveRev":"You may be pouring so much care into a partner or family that you have little left for yourself, or feeling insecure and watchful about where you stand. If you are single, check whether you are giving too much too soon. Balance comes from receiving as well as giving, and from saying what you need out loud.","workUp":"You bring both competence and warmth to your work. Managing resources well, supporting colleagues and creating a stable environment are your strengths now. Practical decisions made with care lead to lasting results. People trust you because you are reliable and kind at the same time, and that combination opens doors.","workRev":"Work demands may be crowding out your personal life, or you are taking care of everyone's problems except your own. Worry about security could be making you overly cautious or suspicious. Set clearer boundaries, delegate where you can, and remember that your time and energy are resources worth protecting too.","picture":"A crowned queen sits on a carved throne in a lush garden, holding a large gold pentacle in her lap and looking down at it tenderly. She wears a red gown with white sleeves, and a long green veil falls from her crown. Red roses climb in an arch over her head, flowers bloom beside her, and blue hills open out behind her under a yellow sky. In the bottom corner a small rabbit sits in the grass. The whole scene feels fertile, sheltered and cared for, a picture of abundance tended by hand."},
"pentacles-14":{"up":"Material success built on sound judgment is within reach, or already in your hands. Here you find mastery of practical life: knowing how to manage resources, make smart decisions, and create stability that others can rely on. The energy is generous and confident without being showy. You may have a good head for numbers, business or planning, and people turn to you for grounded advice. As a person, this may be a successful, dependable figure such as a mentor, boss or provider in your life. As a role, it invites you to own your ability to provide and lead. Enjoy what you have built, and use it well for yourself and those around you.","rev":"Status and possessions may be standing in for something deeper. You or someone around you might be judging worth by money, titles or control, and losing sight of what those things were for. Stubbornness, greed or cutting ethical corners can show up when security becomes the only goal. There can also be a quieter weakness: fear of losing ground that makes a person rigid. As a person, this may be someone powerful who uses resources to dominate rather than support. As a role, check whether that pattern is creeping into your own choices. Real authority rests on integrity. Reconnect with your values and let generosity guide how you use what you have.","loveUp":"Love feels stable and secure. If you are partnered, you may be building a comfortable life together based on loyalty and shared goals. If you are single, you might find yourself drawn to someone dependable and generous. The emphasis is on showing love through steady commitment, practical support and being there when it counts.","loveRev":"Money, control or status may be getting tangled up with love. One partner could be using resources to hold power, or affection might feel conditional on providing. If you are single, notice whether you are drawn to someone for their position more than their character. Real security in love comes from respect, not ownership.","workUp":"Leadership and practical skill are coming together. You may be in a position to manage resources, guide others or grow something successful. Your steady judgment and business sense are valuable. Make decisions with the long term in mind, and share both credit and opportunity with the people around you.","workRev":"Ambition may be tipping into rigidity or a focus on status over substance. Watch for decisions driven by ego or fear of losing control, whether they come from you or from a boss. Ethics matter more than appearances here. Return to what you value, and lead through fairness rather than pressure.","picture":"A king sits on a dark throne carved with bulls' heads, his robe covered in bunches of grapes and vine leaves so thickly that he almost melts into the vineyard around him. One hand holds a scepter topped with a golden orb, and the other rests on a gold pentacle balanced on his knee. A crown sits over a red headdress. Behind him a stone wall and a castle with towers rise against a yellow sky. Grapevines spill over everything, suggesting wealth that has grown, season by season, out of the earth itself."}};
